<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Proof of Theorem 4.1: Decomposition of <math id="A1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{W}_{\rho}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>ρ</mi><mi>W</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{W}_{\rho}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math></h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>A pointwise maximization identity</h3>

<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.1</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Pointwise worst-case Bernoulli perturbation)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix any <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{\star}\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{\star}\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>, any <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[p^{\star}-\rho,p^{\star}+\rho]\subseteq[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[p^{\star}-\rho,p^{\star}+\rho]\subseteq[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>, and any real numbers
<math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a,b\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a,b\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</span></p>
<table id="A1.E26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{p\in[p^{\star}-\rho,p^{\star}+\rho]}\Bigl(p\,a+(1-p)\,b\Bigr)=p^{\star}a+(1-p^{\star})b+\rho\,|a-b|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mo lspace="0em" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{p\in[p^{\star}-\rho,p^{\star}+\rho]}\Bigl(p\,a+(1-p)\,b\Bigr)=p^{\star}a+(1-p^{\star})b+\rho\,|a-b|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Moreover, an optimizer is
<math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{\star}+\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{\star}+\rho</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\geq b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\geq b</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{\star}-\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{\star}-\rho</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a&lt;b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a&lt;b</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">The map <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\mapsto p\,a+(1-p)\,b=b+p(a-b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\mapsto p\,a+(1-p)\,b=b+p(a-b)</annotation></semantics></math> is affine in <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>, hence it attains its maximum over the interval
<math id="A1.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[p^{\star}-\rho,p^{\star}+\rho]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[p^{\star}-\rho,p^{\star}+\rho]</annotation></semantics></math> at an endpoint.
If <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a-b\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a-b\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> the maximizer is <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{\star}+\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{\star}+\rho</annotation></semantics></math>, giving value
<math id="A1.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b+(p^{\star}+\rho)(a-b)=p^{\star}a+(1-p^{\star})b+\rho(a-b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b+(p^{\star}+\rho)(a-b)=p^{\star}a+(1-p^{\star})b+\rho(a-b)</annotation></semantics></math>.
If <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a-b&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a-b&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math> the maximizer is <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{\star}-\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{\star}-\rho</annotation></semantics></math>, giving
<math id="A1.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b+(p^{\star}-\rho)(a-b)=p^{\star}a+(1-p^{\star})b+\rho(b-a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b+(p^{\star}-\rho)(a-b)=p^{\star}a+(1-p^{\star})b+\rho(b-a)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Combining the two cases yields (<a href="#A1.E26" title="Equation 26 ‣ Lemma A.1 (Pointwise worst-case Bernoulli perturbation). ‣ A.1 A pointwise maximization identity ‣ Appendix A Proof of Theorem 4.1: Decomposition of 𝐿^𝑊_𝜌⁢(𝜃) ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">26</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Proof of Theorem 4.1</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Theorem 4.1.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Recall:
(i) the policy-dependent sampling law <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Z}=\mathcal{X}\times\mathcal{Y}\times\mathcal{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Z}=\mathcal{X}\times\mathcal{Y}\times\mathcal{Y}</annotation></semantics></math>
(Eq. (<a href="#S3.E1" title="Equation 1 ‣ 3 Problem Setup ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>),
(ii) the pointwise oracle uncertainty set <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U^{W}(P^{\star},\rho)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><mi>W</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U^{W}(P^{\star},\rho)</annotation></semantics></math> (Eq. (<a href="#S3.E3" title="Equation 3 ‣ 3 Problem Setup ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>)),
(iii) the robust objective <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{W}_{\rho}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>ρ</mi><mi>W</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{W}_{\rho}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> (Eq. (<a href="#S3.E10" title="Equation 10 ‣ Background (SAIL). ‣ 3 Problem Setup ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>)),
and (iv) the SAIL objective <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{\mathrm{SAIL}}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>SAIL</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{\mathrm{SAIL}}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 1: Rewrite the robust objective pointwise in <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(z)</annotation></semantics></math>.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z=(x,y_{1},y_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z=(x,y_{1},y_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(z):=P(1\mid z)=P(y_{1}\succ y_{2}\mid x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≻</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(z):=P(1\mid z)=P(y_{1}\succ y_{2}\mid x)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{\star}(z):=P^{\star}(1\mid z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{\star}(z):=P^{\star}(1\mid z)</annotation></semantics></math>.
By Eq. (<a href="#S3.E3" title="Equation 3 ‣ 3 Problem Setup ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>), <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P\in U^{W}(P^{\star},\rho)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><mi>W</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P\in U^{W}(P^{\star},\rho)</annotation></semantics></math> iff for all <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A1.E27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|p(z)-p^{\star}(z)|\leq\rho." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|p(z)-p^{\star}(z)|\leq\rho.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Assumption 1 ensures <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{\star}(z)\in[\delta,1-\delta]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{\star}(z)\in[\delta,1-\delta]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho\in(0,\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho\in(0,\delta)</annotation></semantics></math>, so
<math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[p^{\star}(z)-\rho,p^{\star}(z)+\rho]\subseteq[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[p^{\star}(z)-\rho,p^{\star}(z)+\rho]\subseteq[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Define the pairwise logit as</p>
<table id="A1.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\theta}(z)\equiv h_{\theta}(x,y_{1},y_{2}):=\log\frac{\pi_{\theta}(y_{1}\mid x)}{\pi_{\mathrm{SFT}}(y_{1}\mid x)}-\log\frac{\pi_{\theta}(y_{2}\mid x)}{\pi_{\mathrm{SFT}}(y_{2}\mid x)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≡</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>SFT</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>SFT</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\theta}(z)\equiv h_{\theta}(x,y_{1},y_{2}):=\log\frac{\pi_{\theta}(y_{1}\mid x)}{\pi_{\mathrm{SFT}}(y_{1}\mid x)}-\log\frac{\pi_{\theta}(y_{2}\mid x)}{\pi_{\mathrm{SFT}}(y_{2}\mid x)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">For notational convenience, set the two label-conditional losses</p>
<table id="A1.E28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{\theta}^{1}(z):=-\log\sigma\bigl(\beta\,h_{\theta}(z)\bigr),\qquad\ell_{\theta}^{0}(z):=-\log\sigma\bigl(\beta\,h_{\theta}(x,y_{2},y_{1})\bigr)=-\log\sigma\bigl(-\beta\,h_{\theta}(z)\bigr)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{\theta}^{1}(z):=-\log\sigma\bigl(\beta\,h_{\theta}(z)\bigr),\qquad\ell_{\theta}^{0}(z):=-\log\sigma\bigl(\beta\,h_{\theta}(x,y_{2},y_{1})\bigr)=-\log\sigma\bigl(-\beta\,h_{\theta}(z)\bigr),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">where we used <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\theta}(x,y_{2},y_{1})=-h_{\theta}(x,y_{1},y_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\theta}(x,y_{2},y_{1})=-h_{\theta}(x,y_{1},y_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Then, for any oracle <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> with Bernoulli parameter <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(z)</annotation></semantics></math>, the conditional risk equals</p>
<table id="A1.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{y\sim P(\cdot\mid z)}\bigl[\ell_{\theta}(z,y)\bigr]=p(z)\,\ell_{\theta}^{1}(z)+(1-p(z))\,\ell_{\theta}^{0}(z)=:\ell\bigl(p(z);h_{\theta}(z)\bigr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{y\sim P(\cdot\mid z)}\bigl[\ell_{\theta}(z,y)\bigr]=p(z)\,\ell_{\theta}^{1}(z)+(1-p(z))\,\ell_{\theta}^{0}(z)=:\ell\bigl(p(z);h_{\theta}(z)\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Therefore <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{W}_{\rho}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>ρ</mi><mi>W</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{W}_{\rho}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> can be written as</p>
<table id="A1.E29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{W}_{\rho}(\theta)=\sup_{P\in U^{W}(P^{\star},\rho)}\ \mathbb{E}_{z\sim d_{\theta}}\Bigl[p(z)\,\ell_{\theta}^{1}(z)+(1-p(z))\,\ell_{\theta}^{0}(z)\Bigr]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>ρ</mi><mi>W</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><mi>W</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{W}_{\rho}(\theta)=\sup_{P\in U^{W}(P^{\star},\rho)}\ \mathbb{E}_{z\sim d_{\theta}}\Bigl[p(z)\,\ell_{\theta}^{1}(z)+(1-p(z))\,\ell_{\theta}^{0}(z)\Bigr].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Because the constraint (<a href="#A1.E27" title="Equation 27 ‣ Step 1: Rewrite the robust objective pointwise in 𝑝(𝑧). ‣ A.2 Proof of Theorem 4.1 ‣ Appendix A Proof of Theorem 4.1: Decomposition of 𝐿^𝑊_𝜌⁢(𝜃) ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">27</span></a>) is pointwise in <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math> and the objective is an integral (expectation)
of a pointwise affine function of <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(z)</annotation></semantics></math>, the worst-case oracle can be chosen pointwise in <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math>.
Equivalently, the supremum in (<a href="#A1.E29" title="Equation 29 ‣ Step 1: Rewrite the robust objective pointwise in 𝑝(𝑧). ‣ A.2 Proof of Theorem 4.1 ‣ Appendix A Proof of Theorem 4.1: Decomposition of 𝐿^𝑊_𝜌⁢(𝜃) ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">29</span></a>) equals the expectation of the pointwise supremum:</p>
<table id="A1.E30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{W}_{\rho}(\theta)=\mathbb{E}_{z\sim d_{\theta}}\left[\ \sup_{p\in[p^{\star}(z)-\rho,\,p^{\star}(z)+\rho]}\Bigl(p\,\ell_{\theta}^{1}(z)+(1-p)\,\ell_{\theta}^{0}(z)\Bigr)\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>ρ</mi><mi>W</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">[</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{W}_{\rho}(\theta)=\mathbb{E}_{z\sim d_{\theta}}\left[\ \sup_{p\in[p^{\star}(z)-\rho,\,p^{\star}(z)+\rho]}\Bigl(p\,\ell_{\theta}^{1}(z)+(1-p)\,\ell_{\theta}^{0}(z)\Bigr)\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">By Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma A.1 (Pointwise worst-case Bernoulli perturbation). ‣ A.1 A pointwise maximization identity ‣ Appendix A Proof of Theorem 4.1: Decomposition of 𝐿^𝑊_𝜌⁢(𝜃) ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>, an optimizer is always an endpoint, hence a measurable selector can be obtained
by taking <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(z)=p^{\star}(z)+\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(z)=p^{\star}(z)+\rho</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{\theta}^{1}(z)\geq\ell_{\theta}^{0}(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{\theta}^{1}(z)\geq\ell_{\theta}^{0}(z)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(z)=p^{\star}(z)-\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(z)=p^{\star}(z)-\rho</annotation></semantics></math> otherwise.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Apply Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma A.1 (Pointwise worst-case Bernoulli perturbation). ‣ A.1 A pointwise maximization identity ‣ Appendix A Proof of Theorem 4.1: Decomposition of 𝐿^𝑊_𝜌⁢(𝜃) ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a> to (<a href="#A1.E30" title="Equation 30 ‣ Step 1: Rewrite the robust objective pointwise in 𝑝(𝑧). ‣ A.2 Proof of Theorem 4.1 ‣ Appendix A Proof of Theorem 4.1: Decomposition of 𝐿^𝑊_𝜌⁢(𝜃) ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">30</span></a>) with
<math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a=\ell_{\theta}^{1}(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a=\ell_{\theta}^{1}(z)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b=\ell_{\theta}^{0}(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b=\ell_{\theta}^{0}(z)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{\star}=p^{\star}(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{\star}=p^{\star}(z)</annotation></semantics></math>. This gives</p>
<table id="A1.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle L^{W}_{\rho}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>ρ</mi><mi>W</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle L^{W}_{\rho}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E31.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{z\sim d_{\theta}}\Bigl[p^{\star}(z)\,\ell_{\theta}^{1}(z)+(1-p^{\star}(z))\,\ell_{\theta}^{0}(z)\Bigr]+\rho\,\mathbb{E}_{z\sim d_{\theta}}\Bigl[|\ell_{\theta}^{1}(z)-\ell_{\theta}^{0}(z)|\Bigr]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{z\sim d_{\theta}}\Bigl[p^{\star}(z)\,\ell_{\theta}^{1}(z)+(1-p^{\star}(z))\,\ell_{\theta}^{0}(z)\Bigr]+\rho\,\mathbb{E}_{z\sim d_{\theta}}\Bigl[|\ell_{\theta}^{1}(z)-\ell_{\theta}^{0}(z)|\Bigr].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.2" class="ltx_p">The first expectation in (<a href="#A1.E31" title="Equation 31 ‣ Step 1: Rewrite the robust objective pointwise in 𝑝(𝑧). ‣ A.2 Proof of Theorem 4.1 ‣ Appendix A Proof of Theorem 4.1: Decomposition of 𝐿^𝑊_𝜌⁢(𝜃) ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">31</span></a>) is exactly <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{\mathrm{SAIL}}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>SAIL</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{\mathrm{SAIL}}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">For the second term, use the identity</p>
<table id="A1.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\sigma(t)-\log\sigma(-t)=t\quad\text{(since $\sigma(t)/\sigma(-t)=e^{t}$).}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mtext>(since </mtext><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow><mtext>).</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\sigma(t)-\log\sigma(-t)=t\quad\text{(since $\sigma(t)/\sigma(-t)=e^{t}$).}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p6.2" class="ltx_p">With <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=\beta h_{\theta}(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=\beta h_{\theta}(z)</annotation></semantics></math> and definitions (<a href="#A1.E28" title="Equation 28 ‣ Step 1: Rewrite the robust objective pointwise in 𝑝(𝑧). ‣ A.2 Proof of Theorem 4.1 ‣ Appendix A Proof of Theorem 4.1: Decomposition of 𝐿^𝑊_𝜌⁢(𝜃) ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">28</span></a>), we obtain</p>
<table id="A1.Ex34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{\theta}^{1}(z)-\ell_{\theta}^{0}(z)=-\log\sigma(\beta h_{\theta}(z))+\log\sigma(-\beta h_{\theta}(z))=-\beta h_{\theta}(z)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{\theta}^{1}(z)-\ell_{\theta}^{0}(z)=-\log\sigma(\beta h_{\theta}(z))+\log\sigma(-\beta h_{\theta}(z))=-\beta h_{\theta}(z).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p6.3" class="ltx_p">Hence <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\ell_{\theta}^{1}(z)-\ell_{\theta}^{0}(z)|=\beta|h_{\theta}(z)|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\ell_{\theta}^{1}(z)-\ell_{\theta}^{0}(z)|=\beta|h_{\theta}(z)|</annotation></semantics></math>, and (<a href="#A1.E31" title="Equation 31 ‣ Step 1: Rewrite the robust objective pointwise in 𝑝(𝑧). ‣ A.2 Proof of Theorem 4.1 ‣ Appendix A Proof of Theorem 4.1: Decomposition of 𝐿^𝑊_𝜌⁢(𝜃) ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">31</span></a>) becomes</p>
<table id="A1.E32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{W}_{\rho}(\theta)=L_{\mathrm{SAIL}}(\theta)+\rho\beta\,\mathbb{E}_{z\sim d_{\theta}}\bigl[|h_{\theta}(z)|\bigr]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>ρ</mi><mi>W</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>SAIL</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{W}_{\rho}(\theta)=L_{\mathrm{SAIL}}(\theta)+\rho\beta\,\mathbb{E}_{z\sim d_{\theta}}\bigl[|h_{\theta}(z)|\bigr].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p6.4" class="ltx_p">Define <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda:=\rho\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda:=\rho\beta</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Under Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption2" title="Assumption 2 (Log-linear policy class). ‣ 4.1 Decomposition of 𝐿^𝑊_𝜌⁢(𝜃) ‣ 4 Proposed Approach ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, for fixed <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> we have the log-linear / softmax form</p>
<table id="A1.Ex35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}(y\mid x)=\frac{\exp(\theta^{\top}\psi(x,y))}{\sum_{y^{\prime}\in\mathcal{Y}}\exp(\theta^{\top}\psi(x,y^{\prime}))}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}(y\mid x)=\frac{\exp(\theta^{\top}\psi(x,y))}{\sum_{y^{\prime}\in\mathcal{Y}}\exp(\theta^{\top}\psi(x,y^{\prime}))}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p7.2" class="ltx_p">By Eq. (<a href="#S4.E11" title="Equation 11 ‣ 4.1 Decomposition of 𝐿^𝑊_𝜌⁢(𝜃) ‣ 4 Proposed Approach ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>), <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\mathrm{SFT}}=\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{ref}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>SFT</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\mathrm{SFT}}=\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{ref}}}</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{\mathrm{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{\mathrm{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then</p>
<table id="A1.Ex36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\log\frac{\pi_{\theta}(y\mid x)}{\pi_{\mathrm{SFT}}(y\mid x)}=(\theta-\theta_{\mathrm{ref}})^{\top}\psi(x,y)-\log\sum_{y^{\prime}}e^{\theta^{\top}\psi(x,y^{\prime})}+\log\sum_{y^{\prime}}e^{\theta_{\mathrm{ref}}^{\top}\psi(x,y^{\prime})}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>SFT</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>log</mi><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></munder><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>log</mi><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></munder><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>ref</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\frac{\pi_{\theta}(y\mid x)}{\pi_{\mathrm{SFT}}(y\mid x)}=(\theta-\theta_{\mathrm{ref}})^{\top}\psi(x,y)-\log\sum_{y^{\prime}}e^{\theta^{\top}\psi(x,y^{\prime})}+\log\sum_{y^{\prime}}e^{\theta_{\mathrm{ref}}^{\top}\psi(x,y^{\prime})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p7.3" class="ltx_p">Taking the difference between <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> cancels the log-partition terms, yielding</p>
<table id="A1.E33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\theta}(x,y_{1},y_{2})=(\theta-\theta_{\mathrm{ref}})^{\top}\bigl(\psi(x,y_{1})-\psi(x,y_{2})\bigr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\theta}(x,y_{1},y_{2})=(\theta-\theta_{\mathrm{ref}})^{\top}\bigl(\psi(x,y_{1})-\psi(x,y_{2})\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(33)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p8.1" class="ltx_p">Then (<a href="#A1.E33" title="Equation 33 ‣ Step 1: Rewrite the robust objective pointwise in 𝑝(𝑧). ‣ A.2 Proof of Theorem 4.1 ‣ Appendix A Proof of Theorem 4.1: Decomposition of 𝐿^𝑊_𝜌⁢(𝜃) ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">33</span></a>) shows <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\theta}(z)=R(\theta;x,y_{1},y_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\theta}(z)=R(\theta;x,y_{1},y_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(\theta;x,y_{1},y_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(\theta;x,y_{1},y_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> is defined in Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 4.1 (Decomposition of 𝐿^𝑊_𝜌⁢(𝜃)). ‣ 4.1 Decomposition of 𝐿^𝑊_𝜌⁢(𝜃) ‣ 4 Proposed Approach ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>, and thus the robust correction term in (<a href="#A1.E32" title="Equation 32 ‣ Step 1: Rewrite the robust objective pointwise in 𝑝(𝑧). ‣ A.2 Proof of Theorem 4.1 ‣ Appendix A Proof of Theorem 4.1: Decomposition of 𝐿^𝑊_𝜌⁢(𝜃) ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">32</span></a>)
is precisely <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda R(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda R(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> with</p>
<table id="A1.Ex37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(\theta):=\mathbb{E}_{z\sim d_{\theta}}\bigl[|R(\theta;x,y_{1},y_{2})|\bigr]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(\theta):=\mathbb{E}_{z\sim d_{\theta}}\bigl[|R(\theta;x,y_{1},y_{2})|\bigr].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p8.2" class="ltx_p">Substituting into (<a href="#A1.E32" title="Equation 32 ‣ Step 1: Rewrite the robust objective pointwise in 𝑝(𝑧). ‣ A.2 Proof of Theorem 4.1 ‣ Appendix A Proof of Theorem 4.1: Decomposition of 𝐿^𝑊_𝜌⁢(𝜃) ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">32</span></a>) gives the claimed decomposition</p>
<table id="A1.Ex38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{W}_{\rho}(\theta)=L_{\mathrm{SAIL}}(\theta)+\lambda R(\theta),\qquad\lambda=\rho\beta." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>ρ</mi><mi>W</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>SAIL</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{W}_{\rho}(\theta)=L_{\mathrm{SAIL}}(\theta)+\lambda R(\theta),\qquad\lambda=\rho\beta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p8.3" class="ltx_p">This completes the proof.
∎</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Weak convexity: Proofs of Theorems 4.7 and 4.8</h2>

<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Auxiliary lemmas</h3>

<div id="A2.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.1</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Policy-regularity constants for the log-linear policy class)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assume Assumption 2 (log-linear / softmax policy class) and Assumption 4 (finite response set and bounded features).
Define the policy score <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\theta}(x,y):=\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(y\mid x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\theta}(x,y):=\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(y\mid x)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then for all <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta,\theta^{\prime}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta,\theta^{\prime}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and all <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,y)\in\mathcal{X}\times\mathcal{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,y)\in\mathcal{X}\times\mathcal{Y}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|g_{\theta}(x,y)\|_{2}\leq G,\qquad\|g_{\theta}(x,y)-g_{\theta^{\prime}}(x,y)\|_{2}\leq M\|\theta-\theta^{\prime}\|_{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|g_{\theta}(x,y)\|_{2}\leq G,\qquad\|g_{\theta}(x,y)-g_{\theta^{\prime}}(x,y)\|_{2}\leq M\|\theta-\theta^{\prime}\|_{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">with explicit constants <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G:=2B_{\psi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G:=2B_{\psi}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M:=B_{\psi}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>:=</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M:=B_{\psi}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Moreover, for <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z=(x,y_{1},y_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z=(x,y_{1},y_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\theta}(z)=\mu(x)\pi_{\theta}(y_{1}\mid x)\pi_{\theta}(y_{2}\mid x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\theta}(z)=\mu(x)\pi_{\theta}(y_{1}\mid x)\pi_{\theta}(y_{2}\mid x)</annotation></semantics></math>, define score <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib47" title="" class="ltx_ref">46</a>]</cite></span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{\theta}(z):=\nabla_{\theta}\log d_{\theta}(z)=g_{\theta}(x,y_{1})+g_{\theta}(x,y_{2})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{\theta}(z):=\nabla_{\theta}\log d_{\theta}(z)=g_{\theta}(x,y_{1})+g_{\theta}(x,y_{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|S_{\theta}(z)\|_{2}\leq 2G=4B_{\psi},\qquad\|\nabla_{\theta}S_{\theta}(z)\|_{\mathrm{op}}\leq 2M=2B_{\psi}^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|S_{\theta}(z)\|_{2}\leq 2G=4B_{\psi},\qquad\|\nabla_{\theta}S_{\theta}(z)\|_{\mathrm{op}}\leq 2M=2B_{\psi}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Under Assumption 2, for fixed <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> the policy is</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}(y\mid x)=\frac{\exp(\theta^{\top}\psi(x,y))}{\sum_{y^{\prime}\in\mathcal{Y}}\exp(\theta^{\top}\psi(x,y^{\prime}))}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}(y\mid x)=\frac{\exp(\theta^{\top}\psi(x,y))}{\sum_{y^{\prime}\in\mathcal{Y}}\exp(\theta^{\top}\psi(x,y^{\prime}))}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">Hence</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\log\pi_{\theta}(y\mid x)=\theta^{\top}\psi(x,y)-\log\sum_{y^{\prime}\in\mathcal{Y}}e^{\theta^{\top}\psi(x,y^{\prime})}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>log</mi><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></munder><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\pi_{\theta}(y\mid x)=\theta^{\top}\psi(x,y)-\log\sum_{y^{\prime}\in\mathcal{Y}}e^{\theta^{\top}\psi(x,y^{\prime})},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">so differentiating gives</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="g_{\theta}(x,y)=\psi(x,y)-\sum_{y^{\prime}\in\mathcal{Y}}\pi_{\theta}(y^{\prime}\mid x)\psi(x,y^{\prime})=\psi(x,y)-\mu_{\theta}(x),\quad\mu_{\theta}(x):=\mathbb{E}_{y^{\prime}\sim\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid x)}[\psi(x,y^{\prime})]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\theta}(x,y)=\psi(x,y)-\sum_{y^{\prime}\in\mathcal{Y}}\pi_{\theta}(y^{\prime}\mid x)\psi(x,y^{\prime})=\psi(x,y)-\mu_{\theta}(x),\quad\mu_{\theta}(x):=\mathbb{E}_{y^{\prime}\sim\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid x)}[\psi(x,y^{\prime})].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text">By Assumption 4, <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\psi(x,y)\|_{2}\leq B_{\psi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\psi(x,y)\|_{2}\leq B_{\psi}</annotation></semantics></math> and Jensen implies <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mu_{\theta}(x)\|_{2}\leq B_{\psi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mu_{\theta}(x)\|_{2}\leq B_{\psi}</annotation></semantics></math>,
hence <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|g_{\theta}(x,y)\|_{2}\leq 2B_{\psi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|g_{\theta}(x,y)\|_{2}\leq 2B_{\psi}</annotation></semantics></math>. This gives <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G:=2B_{\psi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G:=2B_{\psi}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Next, <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta}g_{\theta}(x,y)=-\nabla_{\theta}\mu_{\theta}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta}g_{\theta}(x,y)=-\nabla_{\theta}\mu_{\theta}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>.
A standard calculation yields that the Jacobian of <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\theta}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\theta}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> is the covariance matrix</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\nabla_{\theta}\mu_{\theta}(x)=\mathrm{Cov}_{y^{\prime}\sim\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid x)}\!\bigl(\psi(x,y^{\prime})\bigr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>Cov</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta}\mu_{\theta}(x)=\mathrm{Cov}_{y^{\prime}\sim\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid x)}\!\bigl(\psi(x,y^{\prime})\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">For any unit vector <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\top}\nabla_{\theta}\mu_{\theta}(x)v=\mathrm{Var}\bigl(v^{\top}\psi(x,y^{\prime})\bigr)\leq\mathbb{E}\bigl[(v^{\top}\psi(x,y^{\prime}))^{2}\bigr]\leq\mathbb{E}\|\psi(x,y^{\prime})\|_{2}^{2}\leq B_{\psi}^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\top}\nabla_{\theta}\mu_{\theta}(x)v=\mathrm{Var}\bigl(v^{\top}\psi(x,y^{\prime})\bigr)\leq\mathbb{E}\bigl[(v^{\top}\psi(x,y^{\prime}))^{2}\bigr]\leq\mathbb{E}\|\psi(x,y^{\prime})\|_{2}^{2}\leq B_{\psi}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">Taking the supremum over <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|v\|_{2}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|v\|_{2}=1</annotation></semantics></math> yields <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\nabla_{\theta}\mu_{\theta}(x)\|_{\mathrm{op}}\leq B_{\psi}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla_{\theta}\mu_{\theta}(x)\|_{\mathrm{op}}\leq B_{\psi}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>,
so <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\nabla_{\theta}g_{\theta}(x,y)\|_{\mathrm{op}}\leq B_{\psi}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla_{\theta}g_{\theta}(x,y)\|_{\mathrm{op}}\leq B_{\psi}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> as well. By the mean value theorem,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|g_{\theta}(x,y)-g_{\theta^{\prime}}(x,y)\|_{2}\leq B_{\psi}^{2}\|\theta-\theta^{\prime}\|_{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|g_{\theta}(x,y)-g_{\theta^{\prime}}(x,y)\|_{2}\leq B_{\psi}^{2}\|\theta-\theta^{\prime}\|_{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">so we may take <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M:=B_{\psi}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>:=</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M:=B_{\psi}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, since <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{\theta}(z)=g_{\theta}(x,y_{1})+g_{\theta}(x,y_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{\theta}(z)=g_{\theta}(x,y_{1})+g_{\theta}(x,y_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>, the bounds
<math id="A2.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|S_{\theta}(z)\|_{2}\leq 2G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|S_{\theta}(z)\|_{2}\leq 2G</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\nabla_{\theta}S_{\theta}(z)\|_{\mathrm{op}}\leq 2M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla_{\theta}S_{\theta}(z)\|_{\mathrm{op}}\leq 2M</annotation></semantics></math> follow by triangle inequality.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.2</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Bounded Fisher information)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Define the Fisher information matrix</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex48" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{F}(\theta):=\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mu,\ y\sim\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid x)}\bigl[g_{\theta}(x,y)g_{\theta}(x,y)^{\top}\bigr]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo rspace="0.577em">,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}(\theta):=\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mu,\ y\sim\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid x)}\bigl[g_{\theta}(x,y)g_{\theta}(x,y)^{\top}\bigr].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathcal{F}(\theta)\|_{\mathrm{op}}\leq G^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathcal{F}(\theta)\|_{\mathrm{op}}\leq G^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\in\Theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\in\Theta</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">For any unit vector <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex49" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u^{\top}\mathcal{F}(\theta)u=\mathbb{E}\bigl[\langle u,g_{\theta}(x,y)\rangle^{2}\bigr]\leq\mathbb{E}\bigl[\|g_{\theta}(x,y)\|_{2}^{2}\bigr]\leq G^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u^{\top}\mathcal{F}(\theta)u=\mathbb{E}\bigl[\langle u,g_{\theta}(x,y)\rangle^{2}\bigr]\leq\mathbb{E}\bigl[\|g_{\theta}(x,y)\|_{2}^{2}\bigr]\leq G^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Taking the supremum over <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|u\|_{2}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|u\|_{2}=1</annotation></semantics></math> yields <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathcal{F}(\theta)\|_{\mathrm{op}}\leq G^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathcal{F}(\theta)\|_{\mathrm{op}}\leq G^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Remark B.3</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the weak convexity analysis of <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math>,
we differentiate an expectation taken under the <em id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>-dependent</em> law <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The resulting Hessian formula contains curvature terms involving the score and its Jacobian,
notably <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\varepsilon,\theta}(z)\,\nabla_{\theta}S_{\theta}(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\varepsilon,\theta}(z)\,\nabla_{\theta}S_{\theta}(z)</annotation></semantics></math> where
<math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{\theta}(z)=\nabla_{\theta}\log d_{\theta}(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{\theta}(z)=\nabla_{\theta}\log d_{\theta}(z)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\varepsilon,\theta}(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\varepsilon,\theta}(z)</annotation></semantics></math> is a smoothed absolute value.
To obtain a <em id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">uniform</em> lower bound <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla^{2}R_{\varepsilon}(\theta)\succeq-\kappa_{\varepsilon}I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⪰</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla^{2}R_{\varepsilon}(\theta)\succeq-\kappa_{\varepsilon}I</annotation></semantics></math> (hence weak convexity),
we must control the worst-case quadratic form <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\top}(\nabla_{\theta}S_{\theta}(z))v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\top}(\nabla_{\theta}S_{\theta}(z))v</annotation></semantics></math> uniformly over <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|v\|_{2}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|v\|_{2}=1</annotation></semantics></math>.
This is exactly an operator-norm control. Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma B.2 (Bounded Fisher information). ‣ B.1 Auxiliary lemmas ‣ Appendix B Weak convexity: Proofs of Theorems 4.7 and 4.8 ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a> exemplifies this type of bound
for second-moment (information) matrices, and the proof of Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma B.1 (Policy-regularity constants for the log-linear policy class). ‣ B.1 Auxiliary lemmas ‣ Appendix B Weak convexity: Proofs of Theorems 4.7 and 4.8 ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>
uses the same operator-norm reasoning to bound <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\nabla_{\theta}S_{\theta}(z)\|_{\mathrm{op}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla_{\theta}S_{\theta}(z)\|_{\mathrm{op}}</annotation></semantics></math>,
which is the quantity that directly enters the proof of Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem7" title="Theorem 4.7 (Weak convexity of the robust penalty). ‣ 4.3 Weak convexity of 𝑅(𝜃) ‣ 4 Proposed Approach ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.7</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Proof of Theorem 4.7 (weak convexity of the robust penalty)</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Theorem 4.7.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Recall the robust penalty</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex50" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(\theta):=\mathbb{E}_{z\sim d_{\theta}}\bigl[|R(\theta;x,y_{1},y_{2})|\bigr],\;R(\theta;x,y_{1},y_{2}):=(\theta-\theta_{\mathrm{ref}})^{\top}\bigl(\psi(x,y_{1})-\psi(x,y_{2})\bigr),\quad z=(x,y_{1},y_{2})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(\theta):=\mathbb{E}_{z\sim d_{\theta}}\bigl[|R(\theta;x,y_{1},y_{2})|\bigr],\;R(\theta;x,y_{1},y_{2}):=(\theta-\theta_{\mathrm{ref}})^{\top}\bigl(\psi(x,y_{1})-\psi(x,y_{2})\bigr),\quad z=(x,y_{1},y_{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 1: Smooth approximation.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Fix <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and define <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{\varepsilon}(u):=\sqrt{u^{2}+\varepsilon^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{\varepsilon}(u):=\sqrt{u^{2}+\varepsilon^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Set</p>
<table id="A2.Ex51" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\varepsilon}(\theta):=\mathbb{E}_{z\sim d_{\theta}}\bigl[\phi_{\varepsilon}(s_{\theta}(z))\bigr]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\varepsilon}(\theta):=\mathbb{E}_{z\sim d_{\theta}}\bigl[\phi_{\varepsilon}(s_{\theta}(z))\bigr].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Y}</annotation></semantics></math> is finite, the expectation over <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> is a finite sum, so <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>
is twice continuously differentiable and we may differentiate under the sum.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We will show that <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla^{2}R_{\varepsilon}(\theta)\succeq-\kappa_{\varepsilon}I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⪰</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla^{2}R_{\varepsilon}(\theta)\succeq-\kappa_{\varepsilon}I</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\in\Theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\in\Theta</annotation></semantics></math> with</p>
<table id="A2.E34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{\varepsilon}:=8GB_{\psi}+4MDB_{\psi}+2M\varepsilon," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{\varepsilon}:=8GB_{\psi}+4MDB_{\psi}+2M\varepsilon,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(34)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G,M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G,M</annotation></semantics></math> are as in Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma B.1 (Policy-regularity constants for the log-linear policy class). ‣ B.1 Auxiliary lemmas ‣ Appendix B Weak convexity: Proofs of Theorems 4.7 and 4.8 ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>. Since <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and has a global Hessian lower bound,
the function <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="R_{\varepsilon}(\cdot)+\frac{\kappa_{\varepsilon}}{2}\|\cdot\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\varepsilon}(\cdot)+\frac{\kappa_{\varepsilon}}{2}\|\cdot\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> has positive semidefinite Hessian and is convex;
equivalently, <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>-weakly convex.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 2: Uniform bounds.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Define <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\psi(z):=\psi(x,y_{1})-\psi(x,y_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\psi(z):=\psi(x,y_{1})-\psi(x,y_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>. By Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption4" title="Assumption 4 (Finite response set and bounded features). ‣ 4.3 Weak convexity of 𝑅(𝜃) ‣ 4 Proposed Approach ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex52" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\Delta\psi(z)\|_{2}\leq\|\psi(x,y_{1})\|_{2}+\|\psi(x,y_{2})\|_{2}\leq 2B_{\psi}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\Delta\psi(z)\|_{2}\leq\|\psi(x,y_{1})\|_{2}+\|\psi(x,y_{2})\|_{2}\leq 2B_{\psi}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">By Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption5" title="Assumption 5 (Bounded feasible set). ‣ 4.3 Weak convexity of 𝑅(𝜃) ‣ 4 Proposed Approach ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\theta-\theta_{\mathrm{ref}}\|_{2}\leq D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\theta-\theta_{\mathrm{ref}}\|_{2}\leq D</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\in\Theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\in\Theta</annotation></semantics></math>, hence</p>
<table id="A2.Ex53" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|s_{\theta}(z)|\leq\|\theta-\theta_{\mathrm{ref}}\|_{2}\,\|\Delta\psi(z)\|_{2}\leq 2DB_{\psi}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|s_{\theta}(z)|\leq\|\theta-\theta_{\mathrm{ref}}\|_{2}\,\|\Delta\psi(z)\|_{2}\leq 2DB_{\psi}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Moreover, <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{\varepsilon}(u)\leq|u|+\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{\varepsilon}(u)\leq|u|+\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, so</p>
<table id="A2.E35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq\phi_{\varepsilon}(s_{\theta}(z))\leq 2DB_{\psi}+\varepsilon." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq\phi_{\varepsilon}(s_{\theta}(z))\leq 2DB_{\psi}+\varepsilon.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(35)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 3: Score-function calculus for <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Write <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\theta}(z)=\mu(x)\pi_{\theta}(y_{1}\mid x)\pi_{\theta}(y_{2}\mid x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\theta}(z)=\mu(x)\pi_{\theta}(y_{1}\mid x)\pi_{\theta}(y_{2}\mid x)</annotation></semantics></math> and define the score<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib47" title="" class="ltx_ref">46</a>]</cite></p>
<table id="A2.Ex54" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{\theta}(z):=\nabla_{\theta}\log d_{\theta}(z)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{\theta}(z):=\nabla_{\theta}\log d_{\theta}(z).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Then <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{\theta}(z)=g_{\theta}(x,y_{1})+g_{\theta}(x,y_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{\theta}(z)=g_{\theta}(x,y_{1})+g_{\theta}(x,y_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>, hence Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma B.1 (Policy-regularity constants for the log-linear policy class). ‣ B.1 Auxiliary lemmas ‣ Appendix B Weak convexity: Proofs of Theorems 4.7 and 4.8 ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a> gives</p>
<table id="A2.E36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|S_{\theta}(z)\|_{2}\leq 2G,\qquad\|\nabla_{\theta}S_{\theta}(z)\|_{\mathrm{op}}\leq 2M." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|S_{\theta}(z)\|_{2}\leq 2G,\qquad\|\nabla_{\theta}S_{\theta}(z)\|_{\mathrm{op}}\leq 2M.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(36)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For the integrand <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\varepsilon,\theta}(z):=\phi_{\varepsilon}(s_{\theta}(z))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\varepsilon,\theta}(z):=\phi_{\varepsilon}(s_{\theta}(z))</annotation></semantics></math>, note that</p>
<table id="A2.Ex55" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta}s_{\theta}(z)=\Delta\psi(z),\qquad\nabla_{\theta}r_{\varepsilon,\theta}(z)=\phi_{\varepsilon}^{\prime}(s_{\theta}(z))\,\Delta\psi(z)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta}s_{\theta}(z)=\Delta\psi(z),\qquad\nabla_{\theta}r_{\varepsilon,\theta}(z)=\phi_{\varepsilon}^{\prime}(s_{\theta}(z))\,\Delta\psi(z),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">and since <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\phi_{\varepsilon}^{\prime}(u)|=|u|/\sqrt{u^{2}+\varepsilon^{2}}\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\phi_{\varepsilon}^{\prime}(u)|=|u|/\sqrt{u^{2}+\varepsilon^{2}}\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A2.E37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\nabla_{\theta}r_{\varepsilon,\theta}(z)\|_{2}\leq\|\Delta\psi(z)\|_{2}\leq 2B_{\psi}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla_{\theta}r_{\varepsilon,\theta}(z)\|_{2}\leq\|\Delta\psi(z)\|_{2}\leq 2B_{\psi}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(37)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Also,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex56" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta}^{2}r_{\varepsilon,\theta}(z)=\phi_{\varepsilon}^{\prime\prime}(s_{\theta}(z))\,\Delta\psi(z)\Delta\psi(z)^{\top},\qquad\phi_{\varepsilon}^{\prime\prime}(u)=\frac{\varepsilon^{2}}{(u^{2}+\varepsilon^{2})^{3/2}}\geq 0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>ε</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>ε</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta}^{2}r_{\varepsilon,\theta}(z)=\phi_{\varepsilon}^{\prime\prime}(s_{\theta}(z))\,\Delta\psi(z)\Delta\psi(z)^{\top},\qquad\phi_{\varepsilon}^{\prime\prime}(u)=\frac{\varepsilon^{2}}{(u^{2}+\varepsilon^{2})^{3/2}}\geq 0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.4" class="ltx_p">so <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta}^{2}r_{\varepsilon,\theta}(z)\succeq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⪰</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta}^{2}r_{\varepsilon,\theta}(z)\succeq 0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\theta,z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\theta,z)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Because <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Y}</annotation></semantics></math> is finite, we can differentiate <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\varepsilon}(\theta)=\sum_{z}d_{\theta}(z)\,r_{\varepsilon,\theta}(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>z</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\varepsilon}(\theta)=\sum_{z}d_{\theta}(z)\,r_{\varepsilon,\theta}(z)</annotation></semantics></math>
term-by-term and use <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta}d_{\theta}(z)=d_{\theta}(z)S_{\theta}(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta}d_{\theta}(z)=d_{\theta}(z)S_{\theta}(z)</annotation></semantics></math> to obtain:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla_{\theta}R_{\varepsilon}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla_{\theta}R_{\varepsilon}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E38.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{z\sim d_{\theta}}\bigl[\nabla_{\theta}r_{\varepsilon,\theta}(z)+r_{\varepsilon,\theta}(z)S_{\theta}(z)\bigr]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{z\sim d_{\theta}}\bigl[\nabla_{\theta}r_{\varepsilon,\theta}(z)+r_{\varepsilon,\theta}(z)S_{\theta}(z)\bigr],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(38)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla_{\theta}^{2}R_{\varepsilon}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla_{\theta}^{2}R_{\varepsilon}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E39.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{z\sim d_{\theta}}\Bigl[\nabla_{\theta}^{2}r_{\varepsilon,\theta}(z)+S_{\theta}(z)\nabla_{\theta}r_{\varepsilon,\theta}(z)^{\top}+\nabla_{\theta}r_{\varepsilon,\theta}(z)S_{\theta}(z)^{\top}+r_{\varepsilon,\theta}(z)\bigl(S_{\theta}(z)S_{\theta}(z)^{\top}+\nabla_{\theta}S_{\theta}(z)\bigr)\Bigr]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{z\sim d_{\theta}}\Bigl[\nabla_{\theta}^{2}r_{\varepsilon,\theta}(z)+S_{\theta}(z)\nabla_{\theta}r_{\varepsilon,\theta}(z)^{\top}+\nabla_{\theta}r_{\varepsilon,\theta}(z)S_{\theta}(z)^{\top}+r_{\varepsilon,\theta}(z)\bigl(S_{\theta}(z)S_{\theta}(z)^{\top}+\nabla_{\theta}S_{\theta}(z)\bigr)\Bigr].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(39)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 4: Hessian lower bound.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Fix any unit vector <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Using (<a href="#A2.E39" title="Equation 39 ‣ Step 3: Score-function calculus for 𝑑_𝜃. ‣ B.2 Proof of Theorem 4.7 (weak convexity of the robust penalty) ‣ Appendix B Weak convexity: Proofs of Theorems 4.7 and 4.8 ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">39</span></a>) and the facts that
<math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta}^{2}r_{\varepsilon,\theta}(z)\succeq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⪰</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta}^{2}r_{\varepsilon,\theta}(z)\succeq 0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{\theta}(z)S_{\theta}(z)^{\top}\succeq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>⪰</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{\theta}(z)S_{\theta}(z)^{\top}\succeq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="A2.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex57"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle u^{\top}\nabla_{\theta}^{2}R_{\varepsilon}(\theta)u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle u^{\top}\nabla_{\theta}^{2}R_{\varepsilon}(\theta)u</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex57.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\mathbb{E}_{z\sim d_{\theta}}\Bigl[u^{\top}\bigl(S_{\theta}\nabla_{\theta}r_{\varepsilon,\theta}^{\top}+\nabla_{\theta}r_{\varepsilon,\theta}S_{\theta}^{\top}\bigr)u+r_{\varepsilon,\theta}(z)\,u^{\top}(\nabla_{\theta}S_{\theta}(z))u\Bigr]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\mathbb{E}_{z\sim d_{\theta}}\Bigl[u^{\top}\bigl(S_{\theta}\nabla_{\theta}r_{\varepsilon,\theta}^{\top}+\nabla_{\theta}r_{\varepsilon,\theta}S_{\theta}^{\top}\bigr)u+r_{\varepsilon,\theta}(z)\,u^{\top}(\nabla_{\theta}S_{\theta}(z))u\Bigr].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">For the first term,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex58" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u^{\top}\bigl(S_{\theta}\nabla_{\theta}r_{\varepsilon,\theta}^{\top}+\nabla_{\theta}r_{\varepsilon,\theta}S_{\theta}^{\top}\bigr)u=2\langle u,S_{\theta}(z)\rangle\,\langle u,\nabla_{\theta}r_{\varepsilon,\theta}(z)\rangle\geq-2\|S_{\theta}(z)\|_{2}\,\|\nabla_{\theta}r_{\varepsilon,\theta}(z)\|_{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u^{\top}\bigl(S_{\theta}\nabla_{\theta}r_{\varepsilon,\theta}^{\top}+\nabla_{\theta}r_{\varepsilon,\theta}S_{\theta}^{\top}\bigr)u=2\langle u,S_{\theta}(z)\rangle\,\langle u,\nabla_{\theta}r_{\varepsilon,\theta}(z)\rangle\geq-2\|S_{\theta}(z)\|_{2}\,\|\nabla_{\theta}r_{\varepsilon,\theta}(z)\|_{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.3" class="ltx_p">and using (<a href="#A2.E36" title="Equation 36 ‣ Step 3: Score-function calculus for 𝑑_𝜃. ‣ B.2 Proof of Theorem 4.7 (weak convexity of the robust penalty) ‣ Appendix B Weak convexity: Proofs of Theorems 4.7 and 4.8 ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">36</span></a>) and (<a href="#A2.E37" title="Equation 37 ‣ Step 3: Score-function calculus for 𝑑_𝜃. ‣ B.2 Proof of Theorem 4.7 (weak convexity of the robust penalty) ‣ Appendix B Weak convexity: Proofs of Theorems 4.7 and 4.8 ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">37</span></a>) gives the pointwise bound</p>
<table id="A2.Ex59" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u^{\top}\bigl(S_{\theta}\nabla_{\theta}r_{\varepsilon,\theta}^{\top}+\nabla_{\theta}r_{\varepsilon,\theta}S_{\theta}^{\top}\bigr)u\geq-2(2G)(2B_{\psi})=-8GB_{\psi}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u^{\top}\bigl(S_{\theta}\nabla_{\theta}r_{\varepsilon,\theta}^{\top}+\nabla_{\theta}r_{\varepsilon,\theta}S_{\theta}^{\top}\bigr)u\geq-2(2G)(2B_{\psi})=-8GB_{\psi}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.4" class="ltx_p">For the second term, by (<a href="#A2.E36" title="Equation 36 ‣ Step 3: Score-function calculus for 𝑑_𝜃. ‣ B.2 Proof of Theorem 4.7 (weak convexity of the robust penalty) ‣ Appendix B Weak convexity: Proofs of Theorems 4.7 and 4.8 ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">36</span></a>),
<math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u^{\top}(\nabla_{\theta}S_{\theta}(z))u\geq-\|\nabla_{\theta}S_{\theta}(z)\|_{\mathrm{op}}\geq-2M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u^{\top}(\nabla_{\theta}S_{\theta}(z))u\geq-\|\nabla_{\theta}S_{\theta}(z)\|_{\mathrm{op}}\geq-2M</annotation></semantics></math>,
so with (<a href="#A2.E35" title="Equation 35 ‣ Step 2: Uniform bounds. ‣ B.2 Proof of Theorem 4.7 (weak convexity of the robust penalty) ‣ Appendix B Weak convexity: Proofs of Theorems 4.7 and 4.8 ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">35</span></a>) we have</p>
<table id="A2.Ex60" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\varepsilon,\theta}(z)\,u^{\top}(\nabla_{\theta}S_{\theta}(z))u\geq-(2DB_{\psi}+\varepsilon)\,2M=-4MDB_{\psi}-2M\varepsilon." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn> 2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\varepsilon,\theta}(z)\,u^{\top}(\nabla_{\theta}S_{\theta}(z))u\geq-(2DB_{\psi}+\varepsilon)\,2M=-4MDB_{\psi}-2M\varepsilon.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.5" class="ltx_p">Combining the two bounds and taking expectation yields</p>
<table id="A2.Ex61" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u^{\top}\nabla_{\theta}^{2}R_{\varepsilon}(\theta)u\geq-(8GB_{\psi}+4MDB_{\psi}+2M\varepsilon)=-\kappa_{\varepsilon}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u^{\top}\nabla_{\theta}^{2}R_{\varepsilon}(\theta)u\geq-(8GB_{\psi}+4MDB_{\psi}+2M\varepsilon)=-\kappa_{\varepsilon},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.6" class="ltx_p">for all unit <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math>, hence <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta}^{2}R_{\varepsilon}(\theta)\succeq-\kappa_{\varepsilon}I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⪰</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta}^{2}R_{\varepsilon}(\theta)\succeq-\kappa_{\varepsilon}I</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 5: Pass to the nonsmooth limit <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon\downarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon\downarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math>.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For any <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq\phi_{\varepsilon}(u)-|u|\leq\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq\phi_{\varepsilon}(u)-|u|\leq\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, hence
<math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq R_{\varepsilon}(\theta)-R(\theta)\leq\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq R_{\varepsilon}(\theta)-R(\theta)\leq\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\varepsilon}\to R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\varepsilon}\to R</annotation></semantics></math> uniformly as <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon\downarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon\downarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since each <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>-weakly convex and <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{\varepsilon}\downarrow\kappa_{R}:=8GB_{\psi}+4MDB_{\psi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{\varepsilon}\downarrow\kappa_{R}:=8GB_{\psi}+4MDB_{\psi}</annotation></semantics></math>,
taking <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon\downarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon\downarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math> in the defining weak convexity inequality yields that <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{R}</annotation></semantics></math>-weakly convex.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, by Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma B.1 (Policy-regularity constants for the log-linear policy class). ‣ B.1 Auxiliary lemmas ‣ Appendix B Weak convexity: Proofs of Theorems 4.7 and 4.8 ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>, we may take <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G=2B_{\psi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G=2B_{\psi}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=B_{\psi}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=B_{\psi}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, giving</p>
<table id="A2.Ex62" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{R}\leq 8(2B_{\psi})B_{\psi}+4(B_{\psi}^{2})DB_{\psi}=16B_{\psi}^{2}+4DB_{\psi}^{3}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>ψ</mi><mn>3</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{R}\leq 8(2B_{\psi})B_{\psi}+4(B_{\psi}^{2})DB_{\psi}=16B_{\psi}^{2}+4DB_{\psi}^{3},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p2.2" class="ltx_p">which is the claimed bound in Theorem 4.7.
∎</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.3 </span>Proof of Theorem 4.8</h3>

<div id="A2.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Theorem 4.8.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 4.1 (Decomposition of 𝐿^𝑊_𝜌⁢(𝜃)). ‣ 4.1 Decomposition of 𝐿^𝑊_𝜌⁢(𝜃) ‣ 4 Proposed Approach ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a> we have the exact decomposition</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex63" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{W}_{\rho}(\theta)=L_{\mathrm{SAIL}}(\theta)+\lambda R(\theta),\qquad\lambda=\rho\beta." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>ρ</mi><mi>W</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>SAIL</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{W}_{\rho}(\theta)=L_{\mathrm{SAIL}}(\theta)+\lambda R(\theta),\qquad\lambda=\rho\beta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">Under Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption3" title="Assumption 3 (Smooth SAIL objective). ‣ 4.2 Regularity of of 𝐿^SAIL . ‣ 4 Proposed Approach ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\mathrm{SAIL}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>SAIL</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\mathrm{SAIL}}</annotation></semantics></math> has <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\mathrm{SAIL}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>SAIL</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\mathrm{SAIL}}</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz gradient on <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.
A basic fact is that any <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>-smooth function is <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>-weakly convex. This can be verified directly from the second-order characterization: if <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>-smooth, then <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla^{2}f(\theta)\succeq-LI" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⪰</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla^{2}f(\theta)\succeq-LI</annotation></semantics></math>. Equivalently, the function</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex64" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\;\mapsto\;f(\theta)+\frac{L}{2}\|\theta\|_{2}^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em" stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\;\mapsto\;f(\theta)+\frac{L}{2}\|\theta\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">is convex.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem7" title="Theorem 4.7 (Weak convexity of the robust penalty). ‣ 4.3 Weak convexity of 𝑅(𝜃) ‣ 4 Proposed Approach ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.7</span></a>, <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{R}</annotation></semantics></math>-weakly convex on <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta</annotation></semantics></math>. Scaling preserves weak convexity, so <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda R</annotation></semantics></math>
is <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\lambda\kappa_{R})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\lambda\kappa_{R})</annotation></semantics></math>-weakly convex. Sums of weakly convex functions add their curvature parameters,
hence <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{W}_{\rho}=L_{\mathrm{SAIL}}+\lambda R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>ρ</mi><mi>W</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>SAIL</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{W}_{\rho}=L_{\mathrm{SAIL}}+\lambda R</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>-weakly convex on <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta</annotation></semantics></math> with</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex65" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa:=L_{\mathrm{SAIL}}+\lambda\kappa_{R}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>SAIL</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa:=L_{\mathrm{SAIL}}+\lambda\kappa_{R}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">This concludes the proof of Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem8" title="Theorem 4.8 (Weak convexity of the composite objective ). ‣ 4.3 Weak convexity of 𝑅(𝜃) ‣ 4 Proposed Approach ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.8</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.4 </span>Auxiliary lemma for stochastic gradient oracle</h3>

<div id="A2.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.4</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Second-moment bound for gradient oracle)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix any mini-batch size <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math>, and recall the composite direction in Eq.<a href="#S4.E22" title="Equation 22 ‣ 4.4 Algorithm development ‣ 4 Proposed Approach ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22</span></a>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex66" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G(\theta;Z)\ :=\ G_{\mathrm{SAIL}}(\theta;Z)\ +\ \lambda\,G_{R}(\theta;Z)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>SAIL</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G(\theta;Z)\ :=\ G_{\mathrm{SAIL}}(\theta;Z)\ +\ \lambda\,G_{R}(\theta;Z),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> denotes a generic mini-batch of size <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> drawn i.i.d. from <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> (Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption6" title="Assumption 6 (Stochastic gradient/subgradient oracles). ‣ 4.4 Algorithm development ‣ 4 Proposed Approach ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>).
Under Assumptions <a href="#Thmassumption2" title="Assumption 2 (Log-linear policy class). ‣ 4.1 Decomposition of 𝐿^𝑊_𝜌⁢(𝜃) ‣ 4 Proposed Approach ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, <a href="#Thmassumption4" title="Assumption 4 (Finite response set and bounded features). ‣ 4.3 Weak convexity of 𝑅(𝜃) ‣ 4 Proposed Approach ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, <a href="#Thmassumption5" title="Assumption 5 (Bounded feasible set). ‣ 4.3 Weak convexity of 𝑅(𝜃) ‣ 4 Proposed Approach ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, and <a href="#Thmassumption6" title="Assumption 6 (Stochastic gradient/subgradient oracles). ‣ 4.4 Algorithm development ‣ 4 Proposed Approach ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>, the composite direction has bounded conditional second moment:
for all <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\in\Theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\in\Theta</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex67" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\bigl[\|G(\theta;Z)\|_{2}^{2}\,\big|\,\theta\bigr]\ \leq\ G_{\mathrm{tot}}^{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.337em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.500em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mi>tot</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\bigl[\|G(\theta;Z)\|_{2}^{2}\,\big|\,\theta\bigr]\ \leq\ G_{\mathrm{tot}}^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">with the explicit choice</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex68" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{\mathrm{tot}}^{2}\ :=\ 4\left(G_{\nabla\mathrm{SAIL}}^{2}\;+\;\lambda^{2}\,G_{\partial R}^{2}\;+\;\frac{\sigma_{\mathrm{SAIL}}^{2}+\lambda^{2}\sigma_{R}^{2}}{B}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mi>tot</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.778em">:=</mo><mrow><mn> 4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>SAIL</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>SAIL</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mi>B</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{\mathrm{tot}}^{2}\ :=\ 4\left(G_{\nabla\mathrm{SAIL}}^{2}\;+\;\lambda^{2}\,G_{\partial R}^{2}\;+\;\frac{\sigma_{\mathrm{SAIL}}^{2}+\lambda^{2}\sigma_{R}^{2}}{B}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex69" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{\nabla\mathrm{SAIL}}\ :=\ 2\beta B_{\psi}\;+\;4B_{\psi}\bigl(\log 2+2\beta DB_{\psi}\bigr),\qquad G_{\partial R}\ :=\ 2B_{\psi}\;+\;8DB_{\psi}^{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>SAIL</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.778em">:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn> 2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn> 4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn> 2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn> 8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{\nabla\mathrm{SAIL}}\ :=\ 2\beta B_{\psi}\;+\;4B_{\psi}\bigl(\log 2+2\beta DB_{\psi}\bigr),\qquad G_{\partial R}\ :=\ 2B_{\psi}\;+\;8DB_{\psi}^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\mathrm{SAIL}}^{2},\sigma_{R}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>SAIL</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\mathrm{SAIL}}^{2},\sigma_{R}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> are as in Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption6" title="Assumption 6 (Stochastic gradient/subgradient oracles). ‣ 4.4 Algorithm development ‣ 4 Proposed Approach ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">We bound the deterministic (mean) components <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\nabla L_{\mathrm{SAIL}}(\theta)\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>SAIL</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla L_{\mathrm{SAIL}}(\theta)\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A2.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{dist}(0,\partial R(\theta))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{dist}(0,\partial R(\theta))</annotation></semantics></math>, then combine with the variance bounds in Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption6" title="Assumption 6 (Stochastic gradient/subgradient oracles). ‣ 4.4 Algorithm development ‣ 4 Proposed Approach ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> and the
definition (<a href="#S4.E22" title="Equation 22 ‣ 4.4 Algorithm development ‣ 4 Proposed Approach ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 1: Uniform bounds on the pairwise logit and score.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z=(x,y_{1},y_{2})\in\mathcal{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z=(x,y_{1},y_{2})\in\mathcal{Z}</annotation></semantics></math>, define <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\psi(z):=\psi(x,y_{1})-\psi(x,y_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\psi(z):=\psi(x,y_{1})-\psi(x,y_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>.
By Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption4" title="Assumption 4 (Finite response set and bounded features). ‣ 4.3 Weak convexity of 𝑅(𝜃) ‣ 4 Proposed Approach ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\Delta\psi(z)\|_{2}\leq 2B_{\psi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\Delta\psi(z)\|_{2}\leq 2B_{\psi}</annotation></semantics></math>. Under Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption2" title="Assumption 2 (Log-linear policy class). ‣ 4.1 Decomposition of 𝐿^𝑊_𝜌⁢(𝜃) ‣ 4 Proposed Approach ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>(log-linear policy class),
the pairwise logit admits the cancellation</p>
<table id="A2.Ex70" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\theta}(z)\ =\ h_{\theta}(x,y_{1},y_{2})\ =\ (\theta-\theta_{\mathrm{ref}})^{\top}\Delta\psi(z)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\theta}(z)\ =\ h_{\theta}(x,y_{1},y_{2})\ =\ (\theta-\theta_{\mathrm{ref}})^{\top}\Delta\psi(z)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Hence, by Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption5" title="Assumption 5 (Bounded feasible set). ‣ 4.3 Weak convexity of 𝑅(𝜃) ‣ 4 Proposed Approach ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex71" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex71.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|h_{\theta}(z)|\ \leq\ \|\theta-\theta_{\mathrm{ref}}\|_{2}\;\|\Delta\psi(z)\|_{2}\ \leq\ D\cdot 2B_{\psi}\ =\ 2DB_{\psi}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn> 2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|h_{\theta}(z)|\ \leq\ \|\theta-\theta_{\mathrm{ref}}\|_{2}\;\|\Delta\psi(z)\|_{2}\ \leq\ D\cdot 2B_{\psi}\ =\ 2DB_{\psi}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Moreover, recalling <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\theta}(z)=\mu(x)\pi_{\theta}(y_{1}|x)\pi_{\theta}(y_{2}|x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\theta}(z)=\mu(x)\pi_{\theta}(y_{1}|x)\pi_{\theta}(y_{2}|x)</annotation></semantics></math> (Eq.(<a href="#S3.E1" title="Equation 1 ‣ 3 Problem Setup ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>)) and
<math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{\theta}(z):=\nabla_{\theta}\log d_{\theta}(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{\theta}(z):=\nabla_{\theta}\log d_{\theta}(z)</annotation></semantics></math>, Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma B.1 (Policy-regularity constants for the log-linear policy class). ‣ B.1 Auxiliary lemmas ‣ Appendix B Weak convexity: Proofs of Theorems 4.7 and 4.8 ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a> gives <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|S_{\theta}(z)\|_{2}\leq 4B_{\psi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|S_{\theta}(z)\|_{2}\leq 4B_{\psi}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 2: Uniform bound on <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\nabla L_{\mathrm{SAIL}}(\theta)\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>SAIL</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla L_{\mathrm{SAIL}}(\theta)\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Recall that <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\mathrm{SAIL}}(\theta)=\mathbb{E}_{z\sim d_{\theta}}\bigl[p^{\star}\ell^{1}(h)+(1-p^{\star})\ell^{0}(h)\bigr]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>SAIL</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\mathrm{SAIL}}(\theta)=\mathbb{E}_{z\sim d_{\theta}}\bigl[p^{\star}\ell^{1}(h)+(1-p^{\star})\ell^{0}(h)\bigr]</annotation></semantics></math>,
where <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell^{1}(h)=-\log\sigma(\beta h)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell^{1}(h)=-\log\sigma(\beta h)</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell^{0}(h)=-\log\sigma(-\beta h)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell^{0}(h)=-\log\sigma(-\beta h)</annotation></semantics></math> , and <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{\star}(z)\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{\star}(z)\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>.
Define the pointwise SAIL loss</p>
<table id="A2.Ex72" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex72.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{\theta}(z)\ :=\ p^{\star}(z)\,\ell^{1}\!\bigl(h_{\theta}(z)\bigr)\ +\ (1-p^{\star}(z))\,\ell^{0}\!\bigl(h_{\theta}(z)\bigr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.500em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{\theta}(z)\ :=\ p^{\star}(z)\,\ell^{1}\!\bigl(h_{\theta}(z)\bigr)\ +\ (1-p^{\star}(z))\,\ell^{0}\!\bigl(h_{\theta}(z)\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell^{1}(h)=\log(1+e^{-\beta h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell^{1}(h)=\log(1+e^{-\beta h})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell^{0}(h)=\log(1+e^{\beta h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell^{0}(h)=\log(1+e^{\beta h})</annotation></semantics></math>, we have for all <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max\{\ell^{1}(h),\ell^{0}(h)\}=\log(1+e^{|\beta h|})\leq\log 2+|\beta h|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max\{\ell^{1}(h),\ell^{0}(h)\}=\log(1+e^{|\beta h|})\leq\log 2+|\beta h|</annotation></semantics></math>. Using <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|h_{\theta}(z)|\leq 2DB_{\psi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|h_{\theta}(z)|\leq 2DB_{\psi}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex73" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex73.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\ \leq\ \ell_{\theta}(z)\ \leq\ \log 2+2\beta DB_{\psi}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\ \leq\ \ell_{\theta}(z)\ \leq\ \log 2+2\beta DB_{\psi}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Next, by direct differentiation, the derivatives of <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell^{1},\ell^{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>0</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell^{1},\ell^{0}</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> satisfy
<math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigl|\tfrac{d}{dh}\ell^{1}(h)\bigr|\leq\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigl|\tfrac{d}{dh}\ell^{1}(h)\bigr|\leq\beta</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigl|\tfrac{d}{dh}\ell^{0}(h)\bigr|\leq\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigl|\tfrac{d}{dh}\ell^{0}(h)\bigr|\leq\beta</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>.
Together with <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta}h_{\theta}(z)=\Delta\psi(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta}h_{\theta}(z)=\Delta\psi(z)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\Delta\psi(z)\|_{2}\leq 2B_{\psi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\Delta\psi(z)\|_{2}\leq 2B_{\psi}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex74" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex74.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\nabla_{\theta}\ell_{\theta}(z)\|_{2}\ \leq\ \beta\,\|\Delta\psi(z)\|_{2}\ \leq\ 2\beta B_{\psi}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn> 2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla_{\theta}\ell_{\theta}(z)\|_{2}\ \leq\ \beta\,\|\Delta\psi(z)\|_{2}\ \leq\ 2\beta B_{\psi}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Because <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Y}</annotation></semantics></math> is finite, we may apply the same score-function calculus as in Eq. (<a href="#A2.E38" title="Equation 38 ‣ Step 3: Score-function calculus for 𝑑_𝜃. ‣ B.2 Proof of Theorem 4.7 (weak convexity of the robust penalty) ‣ Appendix B Weak convexity: Proofs of Theorems 4.7 and 4.8 ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">38</span></a>) to write</p>
<table id="A2.Ex75" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex75.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla L_{\mathrm{SAIL}}(\theta)\ =\ \mathbb{E}_{z\sim d_{\theta}}\!\left[\nabla_{\theta}\ell_{\theta}(z)+\ell_{\theta}(z)\,S_{\theta}(z)\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>SAIL</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla L_{\mathrm{SAIL}}(\theta)\ =\ \mathbb{E}_{z\sim d_{\theta}}\!\left[\nabla_{\theta}\ell_{\theta}(z)+\ell_{\theta}(z)\,S_{\theta}(z)\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.5" class="ltx_p">Therefore,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex76" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex76.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\nabla L_{\mathrm{SAIL}}(\theta)\|_{2}\ \leq\ \mathbb{E}_{z\sim d_{\theta}}\!\left[\|\nabla_{\theta}\ell_{\theta}(z)\|_{2}+\ell_{\theta}(z)\,\|S_{\theta}(z)\|_{2}\right]\ \leq\ 2\beta B_{\psi}+\bigl(\log 2+2\beta DB_{\psi}\bigr)\,4B_{\psi}\ =:\ G_{\nabla\mathrm{SAIL}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>SAIL</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn> 2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn> 4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.778em">:</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>SAIL</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla L_{\mathrm{SAIL}}(\theta)\|_{2}\ \leq\ \mathbb{E}_{z\sim d_{\theta}}\!\left[\|\nabla_{\theta}\ell_{\theta}(z)\|_{2}+\ell_{\theta}(z)\,\|S_{\theta}(z)\|_{2}\right]\ \leq\ 2\beta B_{\psi}+\bigl(\log 2+2\beta DB_{\psi}\bigr)\,4B_{\psi}\ =:\ G_{\nabla\mathrm{SAIL}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 3: Uniform bound on <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{dist}(0,\partial R(\theta))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{dist}(0,\partial R(\theta))</annotation></semantics></math>.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Recall <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(\theta)=\mathbb{E}_{z\sim d_{\theta}}[|h_{\theta}(z)|]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(\theta)=\mathbb{E}_{z\sim d_{\theta}}[|h_{\theta}(z)|]</annotation></semantics></math> .
For <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, define the smooth approximation <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi_{\varepsilon}(u):=\sqrt{u^{2}+\varepsilon^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi_{\varepsilon}(u):=\sqrt{u^{2}+\varepsilon^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\varepsilon}(\theta):=\mathbb{E}_{z\sim d_{\theta}}[\varphi_{\varepsilon}(h_{\theta}(z))]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\varepsilon}(\theta):=\mathbb{E}_{z\sim d_{\theta}}[\varphi_{\varepsilon}(h_{\theta}(z))]</annotation></semantics></math>.
As in Eq.(<a href="#A2.E38" title="Equation 38 ‣ Step 3: Score-function calculus for 𝑑_𝜃. ‣ B.2 Proof of Theorem 4.7 (weak convexity of the robust penalty) ‣ Appendix B Weak convexity: Proofs of Theorems 4.7 and 4.8 ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">38</span></a>), we have</p>
<table id="A2.Ex77" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex77.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla R_{\varepsilon}(\theta)\ =\ \mathbb{E}_{z\sim d_{\theta}}\!\left[\nabla_{\theta}r_{\varepsilon,\theta}(z)+r_{\varepsilon,\theta}(z)\,S_{\theta}(z)\right],\qquad r_{\varepsilon,\theta}(z):=\varphi_{\varepsilon}(h_{\theta}(z))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla R_{\varepsilon}(\theta)\ =\ \mathbb{E}_{z\sim d_{\theta}}\!\left[\nabla_{\theta}r_{\varepsilon,\theta}(z)+r_{\varepsilon,\theta}(z)\,S_{\theta}(z)\right],\qquad r_{\varepsilon,\theta}(z):=\varphi_{\varepsilon}(h_{\theta}(z)).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\varphi_{\varepsilon}^{\prime}(u)|\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>φ</mi><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\varphi_{\varepsilon}^{\prime}(u)|\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta}h_{\theta}(z)=\Delta\psi(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta}h_{\theta}(z)=\Delta\psi(z)</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain
<math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\nabla_{\theta}r_{\varepsilon,\theta}(z)\|_{2}\leq\|\Delta\psi(z)\|_{2}\leq 2B_{\psi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla_{\theta}r_{\varepsilon,\theta}(z)\|_{2}\leq\|\Delta\psi(z)\|_{2}\leq 2B_{\psi}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Also, <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq\varphi_{\varepsilon}(u)\leq|u|+\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq\varphi_{\varepsilon}(u)\leq|u|+\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\varepsilon,\theta}(z)\leq 2DB_{\psi}+\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\varepsilon,\theta}(z)\leq 2DB_{\psi}+\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>.
Using <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|S_{\theta}(z)\|_{2}\leq 4B_{\psi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|S_{\theta}(z)\|_{2}\leq 4B_{\psi}</annotation></semantics></math> (Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma B.1 (Policy-regularity constants for the log-linear policy class). ‣ B.1 Auxiliary lemmas ‣ Appendix B Weak convexity: Proofs of Theorems 4.7 and 4.8 ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>), we conclude</p>
<table id="A2.Ex78" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex78.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\nabla R_{\varepsilon}(\theta)\|_{2}\ \leq\ 2B_{\psi}+(2DB_{\psi}+\varepsilon)\,4B_{\psi}\ =\ 2B_{\psi}+8DB_{\psi}^{2}+4\varepsilon B_{\psi}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn> 2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn> 4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn> 2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla R_{\varepsilon}(\theta)\|_{2}\ \leq\ 2B_{\psi}+(2DB_{\psi}+\varepsilon)\,4B_{\psi}\ =\ 2B_{\psi}+8DB_{\psi}^{2}+4\varepsilon B_{\psi}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Hence <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(2B_{\psi}+8DB_{\psi}^{2}+4\varepsilon B_{\psi})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(2B_{\psi}+8DB_{\psi}^{2}+4\varepsilon B_{\psi})</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz on <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta</annotation></semantics></math>.
Moreover, <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\varphi_{\varepsilon}(u)-|u||\leq\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\varphi_{\varepsilon}(u)-|u||\leq\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> implies <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{\theta\in\Theta}|R_{\varepsilon}(\theta)-R(\theta)|\leq\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>sup</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{\theta\in\Theta}|R_{\varepsilon}(\theta)-R(\theta)|\leq\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus for any <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta,\theta^{\prime}\in\Theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta,\theta^{\prime}\in\Theta</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex79" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex79.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|R(\theta)-R(\theta^{\prime})|\ \leq\ |R(\theta)-R_{\varepsilon}(\theta)|+|R_{\varepsilon}(\theta)-R_{\varepsilon}(\theta^{\prime})|+|R_{\varepsilon}(\theta^{\prime})-R(\theta^{\prime})|\ \leq\ 2\varepsilon+\bigl(2B_{\psi}+8DB_{\psi}^{2}+4\varepsilon B_{\psi}\bigr)\,\|\theta-\theta^{\prime}\|_{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0em">+</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn> 2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|R(\theta)-R(\theta^{\prime})|\ \leq\ |R(\theta)-R_{\varepsilon}(\theta)|+|R_{\varepsilon}(\theta)-R_{\varepsilon}(\theta^{\prime})|+|R_{\varepsilon}(\theta^{\prime})-R(\theta^{\prime})|\ \leq\ 2\varepsilon+\bigl(2B_{\psi}+8DB_{\psi}^{2}+4\varepsilon B_{\psi}\bigr)\,\|\theta-\theta^{\prime}\|_{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Letting <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon\downarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon\downarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math> yields that <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{\partial R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{\partial R}</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz on <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e.,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex80" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex80.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|R(\theta)-R(\theta^{\prime})|\;\leq\;G_{\partial R}\|\theta-\theta^{\prime}\|_{2},\qquad\forall\,\theta,\theta^{\prime}\in\Theta," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">∀</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|R(\theta)-R(\theta^{\prime})|\;\leq\;G_{\partial R}\|\theta-\theta^{\prime}\|_{2},\qquad\forall\,\theta,\theta^{\prime}\in\Theta,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">with <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{\partial R}:=2B_{\psi}+8DB_{\psi}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{\partial R}:=2B_{\psi}+8DB_{\psi}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence the local Lipschitz modulus satisfies</p>
<table id="A2.Ex81" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex81.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\limsup_{\theta^{\prime}\to\theta,\;\theta^{\prime}\neq\theta}\frac{|R(\theta^{\prime})-R(\theta)|}{\|\theta^{\prime}-\theta\|_{2}}\;\leq\;G_{\partial R},\qquad\forall\,\theta\in\Theta." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim sup</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">∀</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\limsup_{\theta^{\prime}\to\theta,\;\theta^{\prime}\neq\theta}\frac{|R(\theta^{\prime})-R(\theta)|}{\|\theta^{\prime}-\theta\|_{2}}\;\leq\;G_{\partial R},\qquad\forall\,\theta\in\Theta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p2.3" class="ltx_p">A standard variational-analytic fact for locally Lipschitz functions implies that any (limiting) subgradient is norm-bounded by the local Lipschitz modulus<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">47</a>]</cite>; namely,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex82" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex82.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in\partial R(\theta)\quad\Longrightarrow\quad\|v\|_{2}\leq\limsup_{\theta^{\prime}\to\theta,\;\theta^{\prime}\neq\theta}\frac{|R(\theta^{\prime})-R(\theta)|}{\|\theta^{\prime}-\theta\|_{2}}\leq G_{\partial R}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">∈</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim sup</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in\partial R(\theta)\quad\Longrightarrow\quad\|v\|_{2}\leq\limsup_{\theta^{\prime}\to\theta,\;\theta^{\prime}\neq\theta}\frac{|R(\theta^{\prime})-R(\theta)|}{\|\theta^{\prime}-\theta\|_{2}}\leq G_{\partial R}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p2.4" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial R(\theta)\neq\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial R(\theta)\neq\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\in\Theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\in\Theta</annotation></semantics></math> (Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption6" title="Assumption 6 (Stochastic gradient/subgradient oracles). ‣ 4.4 Algorithm development ‣ 4 Proposed Approach ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>), we conclude</p>
<table id="A2.Ex83" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex83.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{dist}\bigl(0,\partial R(\theta)\bigr)\;\leq\;G_{\partial R},\qquad\forall\,\theta\in\Theta." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">∀</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{dist}\bigl(0,\partial R(\theta)\bigr)\;\leq\;G_{\partial R},\qquad\forall\,\theta\in\Theta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Fix <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\in\Theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\in\Theta</annotation></semantics></math> and abbreviate <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{\mathrm{SAIL}}:=G_{\mathrm{SAIL}}(\theta;Z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>SAIL</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>SAIL</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{\mathrm{SAIL}}:=G_{\mathrm{SAIL}}(\theta;Z)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{R}:=G_{R}(\theta;Z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{R}:=G_{R}(\theta;Z)</annotation></semantics></math>.
By Eq.<a href="#S4.E22" title="Equation 22 ‣ 4.4 Algorithm development ‣ 4 Proposed Approach ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22</span></a> and <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|a+b\|_{2}^{2}\leq 2\|a\|_{2}^{2}+2\|b\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|a+b\|_{2}^{2}\leq 2\|a\|_{2}^{2}+2\|b\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex84" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex84.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\bigl[\|G(\theta;Z)\|_{2}^{2}\mid\theta\bigr]\ \leq\ 2\,\mathbb{E}\bigl[\|G_{\mathrm{SAIL}}\|_{2}^{2}\mid\theta\bigr]\;+\;2\lambda^{2}\,\mathbb{E}\bigl[\|G_{R}\|_{2}^{2}\mid\theta\bigr]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.500em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn> 2</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>SAIL</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn> 2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\bigl[\|G(\theta;Z)\|_{2}^{2}\mid\theta\bigr]\ \leq\ 2\,\mathbb{E}\bigl[\|G_{\mathrm{SAIL}}\|_{2}^{2}\mid\theta\bigr]\;+\;2\lambda^{2}\,\mathbb{E}\bigl[\|G_{R}\|_{2}^{2}\mid\theta\bigr].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">For the SAIL term, write <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{\mathrm{SAIL}}=\nabla L_{\mathrm{SAIL}}(\theta)+(G_{\mathrm{SAIL}}-\nabla L_{\mathrm{SAIL}}(\theta))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>SAIL</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>SAIL</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>SAIL</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>SAIL</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{\mathrm{SAIL}}=\nabla L_{\mathrm{SAIL}}(\theta)+(G_{\mathrm{SAIL}}-\nabla L_{\mathrm{SAIL}}(\theta))</annotation></semantics></math> and apply
<math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|a+b\|_{2}^{2}\leq 2\|a\|_{2}^{2}+2\|b\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|a+b\|_{2}^{2}\leq 2\|a\|_{2}^{2}+2\|b\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> together with Assumption 6:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex85" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex85.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\bigl[\|G_{\mathrm{SAIL}}\|_{2}^{2}\mid\theta\bigr]\ \leq\ 2\|\nabla L_{\mathrm{SAIL}}(\theta)\|_{2}^{2}\;+\;2\,\mathbb{E}\bigl[\|G_{\mathrm{SAIL}}-\nabla L_{\mathrm{SAIL}}(\theta)\|_{2}^{2}\mid\theta\bigr]\ \leq\ 2G_{\nabla\mathrm{SAIL}}^{2}\;+\;2\frac{\sigma_{\mathrm{SAIL}}^{2}}{B}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>SAIL</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.500em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn> 2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>SAIL</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn> 2</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>SAIL</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>SAIL</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.500em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn> 2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>SAIL</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn> 2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>SAIL</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mi>B</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\bigl[\|G_{\mathrm{SAIL}}\|_{2}^{2}\mid\theta\bigr]\ \leq\ 2\|\nabla L_{\mathrm{SAIL}}(\theta)\|_{2}^{2}\;+\;2\,\mathbb{E}\bigl[\|G_{\mathrm{SAIL}}-\nabla L_{\mathrm{SAIL}}(\theta)\|_{2}^{2}\mid\theta\bigr]\ \leq\ 2G_{\nabla\mathrm{SAIL}}^{2}\;+\;2\frac{\sigma_{\mathrm{SAIL}}^{2}}{B}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">For the robust-penalty term, note that for any closed nonempty set <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\subset\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\subset\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and any <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|u\|_{2}\leq\mathrm{dist}(u,A)+\mathrm{dist}(0,A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|u\|_{2}\leq\mathrm{dist}(u,A)+\mathrm{dist}(0,A)</annotation></semantics></math>, hence
<math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|u\|_{2}^{2}\leq 2\,\mathrm{dist}^{2}(u,A)+2\,\mathrm{dist}^{2}(0,A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>dist</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>dist</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|u\|_{2}^{2}\leq 2\,\mathrm{dist}^{2}(u,A)+2\,\mathrm{dist}^{2}(0,A)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Applying this with <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=\partial R(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=\partial R(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> and using Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption6" title="Assumption 6 (Stochastic gradient/subgradient oracles). ‣ 4.4 Algorithm development ‣ 4 Proposed Approach ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> and Step 3 gives</p>
<table id="A2.Ex86" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex86.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\bigl[\|G_{R}\|_{2}^{2}\mid\theta\bigr]\ \leq\ 2\,\mathbb{E}\!\left[\mathrm{dist}^{2}\bigl(G_{R},\partial R(\theta)\bigr)\mid\theta\right]\;+\;2\,\mathrm{dist}^{2}\bigl(0,\partial R(\theta)\bigr)\ \leq\ 2\frac{\sigma_{R}^{2}}{B}\;+\;2G_{\partial R}^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.500em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn> 2</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>dist</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn> 2</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>dist</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.500em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn> 2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mi>B</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mn> 2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\bigl[\|G_{R}\|_{2}^{2}\mid\theta\bigr]\ \leq\ 2\,\mathbb{E}\!\left[\mathrm{dist}^{2}\bigl(G_{R},\partial R(\theta)\bigr)\mid\theta\right]\;+\;2\,\mathrm{dist}^{2}\bigl(0,\partial R(\theta)\bigr)\ \leq\ 2\frac{\sigma_{R}^{2}}{B}\;+\;2G_{\partial R}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Combining the last three displays yields, for all <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\in\Theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\in\Theta</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex87" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex87.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\bigl[\|G(\theta;Z)\|_{2}^{2}\mid\theta\bigr]\ \leq\ 2\left(2G_{\nabla\mathrm{SAIL}}^{2}+2\frac{\sigma_{\mathrm{SAIL}}^{2}}{B}\right)\;+\;2\lambda^{2}\left(2G_{\partial R}^{2}+2\frac{\sigma_{R}^{2}}{B}\right)\ =\ 4\left(G_{\nabla\mathrm{SAIL}}^{2}+\lambda^{2}G_{\partial R}^{2}+\frac{\sigma_{\mathrm{SAIL}}^{2}+\lambda^{2}\sigma_{R}^{2}}{B}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.500em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn> 2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>SAIL</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>SAIL</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mi>B</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn> 2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mi>B</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn> 4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>SAIL</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>SAIL</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mi>B</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\bigl[\|G(\theta;Z)\|_{2}^{2}\mid\theta\bigr]\ \leq\ 2\left(2G_{\nabla\mathrm{SAIL}}^{2}+2\frac{\sigma_{\mathrm{SAIL}}^{2}}{B}\right)\;+\;2\lambda^{2}\left(2G_{\partial R}^{2}+2\frac{\sigma_{R}^{2}}{B}\right)\ =\ 4\left(G_{\nabla\mathrm{SAIL}}^{2}+\lambda^{2}G_{\partial R}^{2}+\frac{\sigma_{\mathrm{SAIL}}^{2}+\lambda^{2}\sigma_{R}^{2}}{B}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p6.2" class="ltx_p">This is exactly the claimed bound with <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{\mathrm{tot}}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mi>tot</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{\mathrm{tot}}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> as stated.
∎</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Moreau envelope and convergence analysis</h2>

<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Proof of Lemma <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem11" title="Lemma 4.11 (Properties of the Moreau envelope ( , )). ‣ 4.4 Algorithm development ‣ 4 Proposed Approach ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.11</span></a> (Properties of the Moreau envelope)</h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem11" title="Lemma 4.11 (Properties of the Moreau envelope ( , )). ‣ 4.4 Algorithm development ‣ 4 Proposed Approach ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.11</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Fix <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}\in(0,1/\kappa)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}\in(0,1/\kappa)</annotation></semantics></math> and recall the definition of the Moreau envelope and proximal point (Definition <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem10" title="Definition 4.10 (Moreau envelope and proximal point). ‣ 4.4 Algorithm development ‣ 4 Proposed Approach ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.10</span></a>)</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex88" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex88.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta):=\min_{u\in\mathbb{R}^{d}}\left\{F(u)+\frac{1}{2\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}\|u-\theta\|_{2}^{2}\right\},\qquad\hat{\theta}=\mathrm{prox}_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}F}(\theta):=\arg\min_{u\in\mathbb{R}^{d}}\left\{F(u)+\frac{1}{2\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}\|u-\theta\|_{2}^{2}\right\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>prox</mi><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></munder></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta):=\min_{u\in\mathbb{R}^{d}}\left\{F(u)+\frac{1}{2\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}\|u-\theta\|_{2}^{2}\right\},\qquad\hat{\theta}=\mathrm{prox}_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}F}(\theta):=\arg\min_{u\in\mathbb{R}^{d}}\left\{F(u)+\frac{1}{2\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}\|u-\theta\|_{2}^{2}\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">1–2. Finiteness, uniqueness, and the gradient formula.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>-weakly convex, the function <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\mapsto F(u)+\frac{\kappa}{2}\|u\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\mapsto F(u)+\frac{\kappa}{2}\|u\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is convex.
Therefore, for any fixed <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>, the function</p>
<table id="A3.Ex89" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex89.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\mapsto F(u)+\frac{1}{2\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}\|u-\theta\|_{2}^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\mapsto F(u)+\frac{1}{2\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}\|u-\theta\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">is <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\frac{1}{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}-\kappa)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\frac{1}{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}-\kappa)</annotation></semantics></math>-strongly convex in <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> (because <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}&lt;1/\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}&lt;1/\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>),
hence it has a unique minimizer <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> and the minimum value <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> is finite.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Moreover, by first-order optimality of <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> for the strongly convex problem,</p>
<table id="A3.E40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\in\partial F(\hat{\theta})+\frac{1}{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\hat{\theta}-\theta),\qquad\text{i.e.,}\qquad\frac{1}{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta-\hat{\theta})\in\partial F(\hat{\theta})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.111em">∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mtext>i.e.,</mtext><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">∈</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\in\partial F(\hat{\theta})+\frac{1}{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\hat{\theta}-\theta),\qquad\text{i.e.,}\qquad\frac{1}{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta-\hat{\theta})\in\partial F(\hat{\theta}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(40)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Standard properties of the Moreau envelope for weakly convex functions imply that <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}</annotation></semantics></math> is
continuously differentiable and that</p>
<table id="A3.Ex90" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex90.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta)=\frac{1}{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta-\hat{\theta})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta)=\frac{1}{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta-\hat{\theta}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Eq. (<a href="#S4.E19" title="Equation 19 ‣ Item 2 ‣ Lemma 4.11 (Properties of the Moreau envelope ( , )). ‣ 4.4 Algorithm development ‣ 4 Proposed Approach ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>) follows immediately:
<math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\theta-\hat{\theta}\|_{2}=\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}\|\nabla F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta)\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\theta-\hat{\theta}\|_{2}=\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}\|\nabla F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta)\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">3. Lipschitz continuity of <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A standard result for <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>-weakly convex <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> is that <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}</annotation></semantics></math> has Lipschitz gradient with constant</p>
<table id="A3.Ex91" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex91.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\mathrm{env}}=\frac{1}{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}(1-\kappa\lambda_{\mathrm{env}})}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>env</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\mathrm{env}}=\frac{1}{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}(1-\kappa\lambda_{\mathrm{env}})},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">which is Eq. (<a href="#S4.E20" title="Equation 20 ‣ Item 3 ‣ Lemma 4.11 (Properties of the Moreau envelope ( , )). ‣ 4.4 Algorithm development ‣ 4 Proposed Approach ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">4. Approximate stationarity of the proximal point.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">By (<a href="#A3.E40" title="Equation 40 ‣ 1–2. Finiteness, uniqueness, and the gradient formula. ‣ C.1 Proof of Lemma (Properties of the Moreau envelope) ‣ Appendix C Moreau envelope and convergence analysis ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">40</span></a>), the vector <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta-\hat{\theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta-\hat{\theta})</annotation></semantics></math> belongs to <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial F(\hat{\theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial F(\hat{\theta})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Therefore</p>
<table id="A3.Ex92" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex92.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{dist}\bigl(0,\partial F(\hat{\theta})\bigr)\leq\left\|\frac{1}{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta-\hat{\theta})\right\|_{2}=\|\nabla F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta)\|_{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{dist}\bigl(0,\partial F(\hat{\theta})\bigr)\leq\left\|\frac{1}{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta-\hat{\theta})\right\|_{2}=\|\nabla F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta)\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">This completes the proof.
∎</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Auxiliary lemmas for Theorem <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 5.2 (Convergence rate for the Moreau envelope). ‣ 5.1 Convergence analysis ‣ 5 Analysis ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.2</span></a> </h3>

<div id="A3.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma C.1</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Monotonicity inequality)<span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assume <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>-weakly convex and let <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}\in(0,1/\kappa)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}\in(0,1/\kappa)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Fix any <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and let</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex93" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex93.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\theta}=\mathrm{prox}_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}F}(\theta),\qquad\xi:=\nabla F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta)=\frac{1}{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta-\hat{\theta})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>prox</mi><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\theta}=\mathrm{prox}_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}F}(\theta),\qquad\xi:=\nabla F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta)=\frac{1}{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta-\hat{\theta}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then for every <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in\partial F(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">∈</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in\partial F(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex94" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex94.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle\xi,v\rangle\geq(1-\kappa\lambda_{\mathrm{env}})\|\xi\|_{2}^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\xi,v\rangle\geq(1-\kappa\lambda_{\mathrm{env}})\|\xi\|_{2}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">By <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>-weak convexity, for all <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x,y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x,y</annotation></semantics></math> and all <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\in\partial F(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">∈</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\in\partial F(x)</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A3.E41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(y)\geq F(x)+\langle g,y-x\rangle-\frac{\kappa}{2}\|y-x\|_{2}^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(y)\geq F(x)+\langle g,y-x\rangle-\frac{\kappa}{2}\|y-x\|_{2}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(41)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">Apply (<a href="#A3.E41" title="Equation 41 ‣ Proof. ‣ C.2 Auxiliary lemmas for Theorem ‣ Appendix C Moreau envelope and convergence analysis ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">41</span></a>) twice:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">(i) with <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=\theta</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y=\hat{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y=\hat{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g=v\in\partial F(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>v</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">∈</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g=v\in\partial F(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A3.E42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(\hat{\theta})\geq F(\theta)+\langle v,\hat{\theta}-\theta\rangle-\frac{\kappa}{2}\|\hat{\theta}-\theta\|_{2}^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(\hat{\theta})\geq F(\theta)+\langle v,\hat{\theta}-\theta\rangle-\frac{\kappa}{2}\|\hat{\theta}-\theta\|_{2}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(42)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">(ii) with <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=\hat{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=\hat{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y=\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y=\theta</annotation></semantics></math>, and any <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{v}\in\partial F(\hat{\theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.111em">∈</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{v}\in\partial F(\hat{\theta})</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A3.E43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(\theta)\geq F(\hat{\theta})+\langle\hat{v},\theta-\hat{\theta}\rangle-\frac{\kappa}{2}\|\theta-\hat{\theta}\|_{2}^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(\theta)\geq F(\hat{\theta})+\langle\hat{v},\theta-\hat{\theta}\rangle-\frac{\kappa}{2}\|\theta-\hat{\theta}\|_{2}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(43)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">By optimality of the proximal point (as in (<a href="#A3.E40" title="Equation 40 ‣ 1–2. Finiteness, uniqueness, and the gradient formula. ‣ C.1 Proof of Lemma (Properties of the Moreau envelope) ‣ Appendix C Moreau envelope and convergence analysis ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">40</span></a>)),
we may choose <math id="A3.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{v}=\frac{1}{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta-\hat{\theta})=\xi\in\partial F(\hat{\theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">∈</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{v}=\frac{1}{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta-\hat{\theta})=\xi\in\partial F(\hat{\theta})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Substituting this choice into (<a href="#A3.E43" title="Equation 43 ‣ Proof. ‣ C.2 Auxiliary lemmas for Theorem ‣ Appendix C Moreau envelope and convergence analysis ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">43</span></a>) gives</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex95" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex95.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(\theta)\geq F(\hat{\theta})+\langle\xi,\theta-\hat{\theta}\rangle-\frac{\kappa}{2}\|\theta-\hat{\theta}\|_{2}^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(\theta)\geq F(\hat{\theta})+\langle\xi,\theta-\hat{\theta}\rangle-\frac{\kappa}{2}\|\theta-\hat{\theta}\|_{2}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Add this inequality to (<a href="#A3.E42" title="Equation 42 ‣ Proof. ‣ C.2 Auxiliary lemmas for Theorem ‣ Appendix C Moreau envelope and convergence analysis ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">42</span></a>) to eliminate <math id="A3.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(\hat{\theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(\hat{\theta})</annotation></semantics></math>, yielding</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex96" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex96.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\geq\langle v,\hat{\theta}-\theta\rangle+\langle\xi,\theta-\hat{\theta}\rangle-\kappa\|\theta-\hat{\theta}\|_{2}^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\geq\langle v,\hat{\theta}-\theta\rangle+\langle\xi,\theta-\hat{\theta}\rangle-\kappa\|\theta-\hat{\theta}\|_{2}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">Rearrange and use <math id="A3.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta-\hat{\theta}=\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}\xi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta-\hat{\theta}=\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}\xi</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex97" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex97.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle\xi,\theta-\hat{\theta}\rangle\leq\langle v,\theta-\hat{\theta}\rangle+\kappa\|\theta-\hat{\theta}\|_{2}^{2}\quad\Longrightarrow\quad\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}\|\xi\|_{2}^{2}\leq\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}\langle v,\xi\rangle+\kappa\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}^{2}\|\xi\|_{2}^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\xi,\theta-\hat{\theta}\rangle\leq\langle v,\theta-\hat{\theta}\rangle+\kappa\|\theta-\hat{\theta}\|_{2}^{2}\quad\Longrightarrow\quad\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}\|\xi\|_{2}^{2}\leq\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}\langle v,\xi\rangle+\kappa\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}^{2}\|\xi\|_{2}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">Divide by <math id="A3.SS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and rearrange:</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex98" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex98.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle v,\xi\rangle\geq(1-\kappa\lambda_{\mathrm{env}})\|\xi\|_{2}^{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle v,\xi\rangle\geq(1-\kappa\lambda_{\mathrm{env}})\|\xi\|_{2}^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p4.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p4.5.1" class="ltx_text">as claimed.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma C.2</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(One-step inequality)<span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assume <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>-weakly convex and bounded below by <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{\inf}&gt;-\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mo>inf</mo></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{\inf}&gt;-\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.
Fix <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}\in(0,1/\kappa)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}\in(0,1/\kappa)</annotation></semantics></math> and define <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\mathrm{env}}:=\frac{1}{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}(1-\kappa\lambda_{\mathrm{env}})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>env</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\mathrm{env}}:=\frac{1}{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}(1-\kappa\lambda_{\mathrm{env}})}</annotation></semantics></math>
as in Lemma <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem11" title="Lemma 4.11 (Properties of the Moreau envelope ( , )). ‣ 4.4 Algorithm development ‣ 4 Proposed Approach ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.11</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consider the projected update (Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ 4.4 Algorithm development ‣ 4 Proposed Approach ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>)</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex99" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex99.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{t+1}:=\mathrm{proj}_{\Theta}\bigl(\theta_{t}-\eta\,G(\theta_{t};Z_{t})\bigr)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>proj</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{t+1}:=\mathrm{proj}_{\Theta}\bigl(\theta_{t}-\eta\,G(\theta_{t};Z_{t})\bigr),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G(\theta_{t};Z_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G(\theta_{t};Z_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\bigl[G(\theta_{t};Z_{t})\mid\theta_{t}\bigr]\in\partial F(\theta_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">∈</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\bigl[G(\theta_{t};Z_{t})\mid\theta_{t}\bigr]\in\partial F(\theta_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then for any stepsize <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex100" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex100.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\bigl[F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta_{t+1})\mid\theta_{t}\bigr]\leq F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta_{t})-\eta(1-\kappa\lambda_{\mathrm{env}})\|\nabla F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta_{t})\|_{2}^{2}+\frac{L_{\mathrm{env}}\eta^{2}}{2}\,\mathbb{E}\bigl[\|G(\theta_{t};Z_{t})\|_{2}^{2}\mid\theta_{t}\bigr]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>env</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\bigl[F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta_{t+1})\mid\theta_{t}\bigr]\leq F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta_{t})-\eta(1-\kappa\lambda_{\mathrm{env}})\|\nabla F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta_{t})\|_{2}^{2}+\frac{L_{\mathrm{env}}\eta^{2}}{2}\,\mathbb{E}\bigl[\|G(\theta_{t};Z_{t})\|_{2}^{2}\mid\theta_{t}\bigr].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Write <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F=L^{W}_{\rho}+I_{\Theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>ρ</mi><mi>W</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F=L^{W}_{\rho}+I_{\Theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{\Theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{\Theta}</annotation></semantics></math> is the indicator of <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta</annotation></semantics></math> (Eq.(<a href="#S4.E16" title="Equation 16 ‣ 4.4 Algorithm development ‣ 4 Proposed Approach ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>)).
Then the envelope can be written as</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex101" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex101.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(z)=\min_{u\in\Theta}\left\{f(u)+\frac{1}{2\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}\|u-z\|_{2}^{2}\right\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(z)=\min_{u\in\Theta}\left\{f(u)+\frac{1}{2\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}\|u-z\|_{2}^{2}\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{z}:=\mathrm{proj}_{\Theta}(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>proj</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{z}:=\mathrm{proj}_{\Theta}(z)</annotation></semantics></math>. For any <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in\Theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in\Theta</annotation></semantics></math>, Euclidean projection optimality implies
<math id="A3.SS2.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle z-\tilde{z},u-\tilde{z}\rangle\leq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle z-\tilde{z},u-\tilde{z}\rangle\leq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, hence</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex102" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex102.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|u-\tilde{z}\|_{2}^{2}=\|u-z+(z-\tilde{z})\|_{2}^{2}=\|u-z\|_{2}^{2}+\|z-\tilde{z}\|_{2}^{2}+2\langle u-z,z-\tilde{z}\rangle\leq\|u-z\|_{2}^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|u-\tilde{z}\|_{2}^{2}=\|u-z+(z-\tilde{z})\|_{2}^{2}=\|u-z\|_{2}^{2}+\|z-\tilde{z}\|_{2}^{2}+2\langle u-z,z-\tilde{z}\rangle\leq\|u-z\|_{2}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">Taking the minimum over <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in\Theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in\Theta</annotation></semantics></math> gives the monotonicity under projection:</span></p>
<table id="A3.E44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\mathrm{proj}_{\Theta}(z))\leq F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(z)\quad\text{for all }z\in\mathbb{R}^{d}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>proj</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext>for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\mathrm{proj}_{\Theta}(z))\leq F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(z)\quad\text{for all }z\in\mathbb{R}^{d}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(44)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now define the unprojected point <math id="A3.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{t}:=\theta_{t}-\eta G(\theta_{t};Z_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{t}:=\theta_{t}-\eta G(\theta_{t};Z_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A3.SS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{t+1}=\mathrm{proj}_{\Theta}(z_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>proj</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{t+1}=\mathrm{proj}_{\Theta}(z_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>.
By (<a href="#A3.E44" title="Equation 44 ‣ Proof. ‣ C.2 Auxiliary lemmas for Theorem ‣ Appendix C Moreau envelope and convergence analysis ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">44</span></a>),</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex103" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex103.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta_{t+1})\leq F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(z_{t})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta_{t+1})\leq F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(z_{t}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">By Lemma <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem11" title="Lemma 4.11 (Properties of the Moreau envelope ( , )). ‣ 4.4 Algorithm development ‣ 4 Proposed Approach ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.11</span></a>, <math id="A3.SS2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A3.SS2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\mathrm{env}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>env</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\mathrm{env}}</annotation></semantics></math>-smooth, hence</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex104" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex104.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta_{t}-\eta G(\theta_{t};Z_{t}))\leq F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta_{t})-\eta\langle\nabla F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta_{t}),G(\theta_{t};Z_{t})\rangle+\frac{L_{\mathrm{env}}\eta^{2}}{2}\|G(\theta_{t};Z_{t})\|_{2}^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>env</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta_{t}-\eta G(\theta_{t};Z_{t}))\leq F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta_{t})-\eta\langle\nabla F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta_{t}),G(\theta_{t};Z_{t})\rangle+\frac{L_{\mathrm{env}}\eta^{2}}{2}\|G(\theta_{t};Z_{t})\|_{2}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p6.3.1" class="ltx_text">Combining with the previous display and taking conditional expectation yields</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex105" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex105.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\bigl[F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta_{t+1})\mid\theta_{t}\bigr]\leq F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta_{t})-\eta\left\langle\nabla F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta_{t}),\ \mathbb{E}[G(\theta_{t};Z_{t})\mid\theta_{t}]\right\rangle+\frac{L_{\mathrm{env}}\eta^{2}}{2}\,\mathbb{E}\bigl[\|G(\theta_{t};Z_{t})\|_{2}^{2}\mid\theta_{t}\bigr]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>env</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\bigl[F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta_{t+1})\mid\theta_{t}\bigr]\leq F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta_{t})-\eta\left\langle\nabla F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta_{t}),\ \mathbb{E}[G(\theta_{t};Z_{t})\mid\theta_{t}]\right\rangle+\frac{L_{\mathrm{env}}\eta^{2}}{2}\,\mathbb{E}\bigl[\|G(\theta_{t};Z_{t})\|_{2}^{2}\mid\theta_{t}\bigr].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p6.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p6.4.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A3.SS2.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{t}:=\mathbb{E}[G(\theta_{t};Z_{t})\mid\theta_{t}]\in\partial F(\theta_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">∈</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{t}:=\mathbb{E}[G(\theta_{t};Z_{t})\mid\theta_{t}]\in\partial F(\theta_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> by assumption.
Applying Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma C.1 (Monotonicity inequality). ‣ C.2 Auxiliary lemmas for Theorem ‣ Appendix C Moreau envelope and convergence analysis ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a> with <math id="A3.SS2.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta=\theta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta=\theta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS2.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi=\nabla F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi=\nabla F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.SS2.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v=v_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v=v_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>
gives <math id="A3.SS2.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle\nabla F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta_{t}),v_{t}\rangle\geq(1-\kappa\lambda_{\mathrm{env}})\|\nabla F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta_{t})\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\nabla F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta_{t}),v_{t}\rangle\geq(1-\kappa\lambda_{\mathrm{env}})\|\nabla F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta_{t})\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Substituting completes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.3 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 5.2 (Convergence rate for the Moreau envelope). ‣ 5.1 Convergence analysis ‣ 5 Analysis ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.2</span></a> (convergence rate of the Moreau envelope)</h3>

<div id="A3.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Theorem <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 5.2 (Convergence rate for the Moreau envelope). ‣ 5.1 Convergence analysis ‣ 5 Analysis ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.2</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Fix <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}\in(0,1/\kappa)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}\in(0,1/\kappa)</annotation></semantics></math> and stepsize <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.
By Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma C.2 (One-step inequality). ‣ C.2 Auxiliary lemmas for Theorem ‣ Appendix C Moreau envelope and convergence analysis ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a>, for each <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex106"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex106.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\bigl[F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta_{t+1})\mid\theta_{t}\bigr]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\bigl[F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta_{t+1})\mid\theta_{t}\bigr]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex106.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta_{t})-\eta(1-\kappa\lambda_{\mathrm{env}})\|\nabla F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta_{t})\|_{2}^{2}+\frac{L_{\mathrm{env}}\eta^{2}}{2}\,\mathbb{E}\bigl[\|G(\theta_{t};Z_{t})\|_{2}^{2}\mid\theta_{t}\bigr]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>env</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta_{t})-\eta(1-\kappa\lambda_{\mathrm{env}})\|\nabla F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta_{t})\|_{2}^{2}+\frac{L_{\mathrm{env}}\eta^{2}}{2}\,\mathbb{E}\bigl[\|G(\theta_{t};Z_{t})\|_{2}^{2}\mid\theta_{t}\bigr].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">Take total expectation and sum from <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=0</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T-1</annotation></semantics></math> to obtain the telescoping inequality</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\eta(1-\kappa\lambda_{\mathrm{env}})\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\mathbb{E}\bigl[\|\nabla F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta_{t})\|_{2}^{2}\bigr]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\eta(1-\kappa\lambda_{\mathrm{env}})\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\mathbb{E}\bigl[\|\nabla F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta_{t})\|_{2}^{2}\bigr]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E45.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta_{0})-\mathbb{E}\bigl[F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta_{T})\bigr]+\frac{L_{\mathrm{env}}\eta^{2}}{2}\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\mathbb{E}\bigl[\|G(\theta_{t};Z_{t})\|_{2}^{2}\bigr]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>env</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta_{0})-\mathbb{E}\bigl[F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta_{T})\bigr]+\frac{L_{\mathrm{env}}\eta^{2}}{2}\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\mathbb{E}\bigl[\|G(\theta_{t};Z_{t})\|_{2}^{2}\bigr].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(45)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta)\geq\inf_{u}F(u)=F_{\inf}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≥</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><mi>u</mi></msub><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mo>inf</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta)\geq\inf_{u}F(u)=F_{\inf}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>, we have
<math id="A3.SS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta_{T})]\geq F_{\inf}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mo>inf</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta_{T})]\geq F_{\inf}</annotation></semantics></math>.
By Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma B.4 (Second-moment bound for gradient oracle). ‣ B.4 Auxiliary lemma for stochastic gradient oracle ‣ Appendix B Weak convexity: Proofs of Theorems 4.7 and 4.8 ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.4</span></a>, <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\|G(\theta_{t};Z_{t})\|_{2}^{2}\leq G_{\mathrm{tot}}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mi>tot</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\|G(\theta_{t};Z_{t})\|_{2}^{2}\leq G_{\mathrm{tot}}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus (<a href="#A3.E45" title="Equation 45 ‣ Proof of Theorem . ‣ C.3 Proof of Theorem (convergence rate of the Moreau envelope) ‣ Appendix C Moreau envelope and convergence analysis ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">45</span></a>) implies</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex107" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex107.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta(1-\kappa\lambda_{\mathrm{env}})\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\mathbb{E}\bigl[\|\nabla F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta_{t})\|_{2}^{2}\bigr]\leq F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta_{0})-F_{\inf}+\frac{L_{\mathrm{env}}\eta^{2}}{2}\,T\,G_{\mathrm{tot}}^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mo>inf</mo></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>env</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mi>tot</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta(1-\kappa\lambda_{\mathrm{env}})\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\mathbb{E}\bigl[\|\nabla F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta_{t})\|_{2}^{2}\bigr]\leq F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta_{0})-F_{\inf}+\frac{L_{\mathrm{env}}\eta^{2}}{2}\,T\,G_{\mathrm{tot}}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text">Divide by <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta(1-\kappa\lambda_{\mathrm{env}})T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta(1-\kappa\lambda_{\mathrm{env}})T</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex108" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex108.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{T}\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\mathbb{E}\bigl[\|\nabla F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta_{t})\|_{2}^{2}\bigr]\leq\frac{F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta_{0})-F_{\inf}}{\eta(1-\kappa\lambda_{\mathrm{env}})T}+\frac{L_{\mathrm{env}}\eta}{2(1-\kappa\lambda_{\mathrm{env}})}\,G_{\mathrm{tot}}^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mo>inf</mo></msub></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>env</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mi>tot</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{T}\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\mathbb{E}\bigl[\|\nabla F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta_{t})\|_{2}^{2}\bigr]\leq\frac{F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta_{0})-F_{\inf}}{\eta(1-\kappa\lambda_{\mathrm{env}})T}+\frac{L_{\mathrm{env}}\eta}{2(1-\kappa\lambda_{\mathrm{env}})}\,G_{\mathrm{tot}}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p1.5.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> be uniformly distributed on <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{0,\dots,T-1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{0,\dots,T-1\}</annotation></semantics></math>, independent of the algorithmic randomness.
Then</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex109" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex109.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\bigl[\|\nabla F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta_{R})\|_{2}^{2}\bigr]=\frac{1}{T}\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\mathbb{E}\bigl[\|\nabla F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta_{t})\|_{2}^{2}\bigr]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\bigl[\|\nabla F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta_{R})\|_{2}^{2}\bigr]=\frac{1}{T}\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\mathbb{E}\bigl[\|\nabla F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta_{t})\|_{2}^{2}\bigr],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p1.6.1" class="ltx_text">and we obtain exactly Eq.(<a href="#S5.E24" title="Equation 24 ‣ Theorem 5.2 (Convergence rate for the Moreau envelope). ‣ 5.1 Convergence analysis ‣ 5 Analysis ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a>) of Theorem <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 5.2 (Convergence rate for the Moreau envelope). ‣ 5.1 Convergence analysis ‣ 5 Analysis ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.2</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Corollary <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem3" title="Corollary 5.3 (Sample complexity for envelope stationarity). ‣ 5.1 Convergence analysis ‣ 5 Analysis ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.3</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Plug the stated stepsize choice</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex110" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex110.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta:=\frac{1}{G_{\mathrm{tot}}}\sqrt{\frac{2\bigl(F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta_{0})-F_{\inf}\bigr)}{L_{\mathrm{env}}T}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>tot</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mo>inf</mo></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>env</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta:=\frac{1}{G_{\mathrm{tot}}}\sqrt{\frac{2\bigl(F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta_{0})-F_{\inf}\bigr)}{L_{\mathrm{env}}T}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">into the right-hand side of Eq.(<a href="#S5.E24" title="Equation 24 ‣ Theorem 5.2 (Convergence rate for the Moreau envelope). ‣ 5.1 Convergence analysis ‣ 5 Analysis ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a>) and simplify to obtain</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex111" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex111.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\bigl[\|\nabla F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta_{R})\|_{2}^{2}\bigr]\leq\frac{2G_{\mathrm{tot}}\sqrt{2L_{\mathrm{env}}\bigl(F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta_{0})-F_{\inf}\bigr)}}{(1-\kappa\lambda_{\mathrm{env}})\sqrt{T}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>tot</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>env</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mo>inf</mo></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>T</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\bigl[\|\nabla F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta_{R})\|_{2}^{2}\bigr]\leq\frac{2G_{\mathrm{tot}}\sqrt{2L_{\mathrm{env}}\bigl(F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta_{0})-F_{\inf}\bigr)}}{(1-\kappa\lambda_{\mathrm{env}})\sqrt{T}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">By Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma B.4 (Second-moment bound for gradient oracle). ‣ B.4 Auxiliary lemma for stochastic gradient oracle ‣ Appendix B Weak convexity: Proofs of Theorems 4.7 and 4.8 ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.4</span></a>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex112" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex112.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{\mathrm{tot}}^{2}\ :=\ 4\left(G_{\nabla\mathrm{SAIL}}^{2}\;+\;\lambda^{2}\,G_{\partial R}^{2}\;+\;\frac{\sigma_{\mathrm{SAIL}}^{2}+\lambda^{2}\sigma_{R}^{2}}{B}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mi>tot</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.778em">:=</mo><mrow><mn> 4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>SAIL</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>SAIL</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mi>B</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{\mathrm{tot}}^{2}\ :=\ 4\left(G_{\nabla\mathrm{SAIL}}^{2}\;+\;\lambda^{2}\,G_{\partial R}^{2}\;+\;\frac{\sigma_{\mathrm{SAIL}}^{2}+\lambda^{2}\sigma_{R}^{2}}{B}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">To ensure that <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\!\left[\|\nabla F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta_{R})\|_{2}^{2}\right]\leq\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\!\left[\|\nabla F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta_{R})\|_{2}^{2}\right]\leq\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, we substitute <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{\mathrm{tot}}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mi>tot</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{\mathrm{tot}}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> into Theorem <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 5.2 (Convergence rate for the Moreau envelope). ‣ 5.1 Convergence analysis ‣ 5 Analysis ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.2</span></a> and obtain that it suffices to take</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex113" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex113X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex113X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle T</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex113X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\ \frac{2\,G_{\mathrm{tot}}^{2}\bigl(F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta_{0})-F_{\inf}\bigr)}{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}(1-\kappa\lambda_{\mathrm{env}})^{3}\,\varepsilon^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.778em">≥</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mi>tot</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mo>inf</mo></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\ \frac{2\,G_{\mathrm{tot}}^{2}\bigl(F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta_{0})-F_{\inf}\bigr)}{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}(1-\kappa\lambda_{\mathrm{env}})^{3}\,\varepsilon^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex113Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex113Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\ \frac{8\left(C+\frac{\sigma_{\mathrm{SAIL}}^{2}+\lambda^{2}\sigma_{R}^{2}}{B}\right)\bigl(F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta_{0})-F_{\inf}\bigr)}{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}(1-\kappa\lambda_{\mathrm{env}})^{3}\,\varepsilon^{2}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>SAIL</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mi>B</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mo>inf</mo></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\ \frac{8\left(C+\frac{\sigma_{\mathrm{SAIL}}^{2}+\lambda^{2}\sigma_{R}^{2}}{B}\right)\bigl(F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta_{0})-F_{\inf}\bigr)}{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}(1-\kappa\lambda_{\mathrm{env}})^{3}\,\varepsilon^{2}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C:=G_{\nabla\mathrm{SAIL}}^{2}+\lambda^{2}G_{\partial R}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>SAIL</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C:=G_{\nabla\mathrm{SAIL}}^{2}+\lambda^{2}G_{\partial R}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>On the practical role of the proximal point</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section provides a practical interpretation of the proximal-point and Moreau-envelope constructions used in our analysis. Throughout, recall the constrained objective</p>
<table id="A4.Ex114" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex114.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(\theta):=L^{W}_{\rho}(\theta)+I_{\Theta}(\theta)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>ρ</mi><mi>W</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(\theta):=L^{W}_{\rho}(\theta)+I_{\Theta}(\theta),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and the envelope parameter <math id="A4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\rm env}\in(0,1/\kappa)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\rm env}\in(0,1/\kappa)</annotation></semantics></math> from Definition <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem10" title="Definition 4.10 (Moreau envelope and proximal point). ‣ 4.4 Algorithm development ‣ 4 Proposed Approach ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.10</span></a>, where <math id="A4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math> is the weak convexity constant from Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem8" title="Theorem 4.8 (Weak convexity of the composite objective ). ‣ 4.3 Weak convexity of 𝑅(𝜃) ‣ 4 Proposed Approach ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.8</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The Moreau envelope</p>
<table id="A4.Ex115" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex115.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{\lambda_{\rm env}}(\theta)\;=\;\min_{u\in\mathbb{R}^{d}}\Big\{F(u)+\tfrac{1}{2\lambda_{\rm env}}\|u-\theta\|_{2}^{2}\Big\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{\lambda_{\rm env}}(\theta)\;=\;\min_{u\in\mathbb{R}^{d}}\Big\{F(u)+\tfrac{1}{2\lambda_{\rm env}}\|u-\theta\|_{2}^{2}\Big\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p2.2" class="ltx_p">can be viewed as a <em id="A4.p2.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">smoothed</em> surrogate of the potentially nonsmooth, nonconvex objective <math id="A4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math>. The quadratic term discourages large moves away from the current iterate <math id="A4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>, and the minimizer of the inner problem—the <em id="A4.p2.2.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">proximal point</em>—acts as a locally stabilized refinement of <math id="A4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>.
Concretely, for any iterate <math id="A4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> we write</p>
<table id="A4.Ex116" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex116.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\theta}:=\operatorname{prox}_{\lambda_{\rm env}F}(\theta)\in\arg\min_{u\in\mathbb{R}^{d}}\Big\{F(u)+\tfrac{1}{2\lambda_{\rm env}}\|u-\theta\|_{2}^{2}\Big\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>prox</mi><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></munder></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\theta}:=\operatorname{prox}_{\lambda_{\rm env}F}(\theta)\in\arg\min_{u\in\mathbb{R}^{d}}\Big\{F(u)+\tfrac{1}{2\lambda_{\rm env}}\|u-\theta\|_{2}^{2}\Big\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Because <math id="A4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A4.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>-weakly convex and <math id="A4.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\rm env}&lt;1/\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\rm env}&lt;1/\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>, the proximal subproblem is strongly convex in <math id="A4.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> and hence has a unique minimizer. This is the fundamental reason the envelope is differentiable and why <math id="A4.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\nabla F_{\lambda_{\rm env}}(\theta)\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla F_{\lambda_{\rm env}}(\theta)\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is a meaningful stationarity proxy (Lemma <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem11" title="Lemma 4.11 (Properties of the Moreau envelope ( , )). ‣ 4.4 Algorithm development ‣ 4 Proposed Approach ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.11</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ 4.4 Algorithm development ‣ 4 Proposed Approach ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> does <em id="A4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">not</em> require solving the proximal subproblem at each iteration. The algorithm updates <math id="A4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> using stochastic subgradient information for <math id="A4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{W}_{\rho}=L_{\mathrm{SAIL}}+\lambda R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>ρ</mi><mi>W</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>SAIL</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{W}_{\rho}=L_{\mathrm{SAIL}}+\lambda R</annotation></semantics></math> followed by projection onto <math id="A4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta</annotation></semantics></math>, and then outputs a random iterate <math id="A4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{R}</annotation></semantics></math>. The proximal point</p>
<table id="A4.Ex117" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex117.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\theta}_{R}:=\operatorname{prox}_{\lambda_{\rm env}F}(\theta_{R})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>prox</mi><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\theta}_{R}:=\operatorname{prox}_{\lambda_{\rm env}F}(\theta_{R})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p3.2" class="ltx_p">is introduced only as a <em id="A4.p3.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">theoretical device</em> to translate envelope stationarity at <math id="A4.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> into near-stationarity of the original constrained objective at <math id="A4.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\theta}_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\theta}_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> (see Lemma <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem11" title="Lemma 4.11 (Properties of the Moreau envelope ( , )). ‣ 4.4 Algorithm development ‣ 4 Proposed Approach ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.11</span></a> and Theorem <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 5.2 (Convergence rate for the Moreau envelope). ‣ 5.1 Convergence analysis ‣ 5 Analysis ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.2</span></a>). In particular, Lemma <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem11" title="Lemma 4.11 (Properties of the Moreau envelope ( , )). ‣ 4.4 Algorithm development ‣ 4 Proposed Approach ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.11</span></a> implies that <math id="A4.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\theta}_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\theta}_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> are close whenever the envelope gradient is small:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex118" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex118.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\theta_{R}-\hat{\theta}_{R}\|_{2}\;=\;\lambda_{\rm env}\,\|\nabla F_{\lambda_{\rm env}}(\theta_{R})\|_{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\theta_{R}-\hat{\theta}_{R}\|_{2}\;=\;\lambda_{\rm env}\,\|\nabla F_{\lambda_{\rm env}}(\theta_{R})\|_{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p3.3" class="ltx_p">and also that <math id="A4.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\theta}_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\theta}_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> is nearly stationary for <math id="A4.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> in the sense that</p>
<table id="A4.Ex119" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex119.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{dist}\bigl(0,\partial F(\hat{\theta}_{R})\bigr)\;\leq\;\|\nabla F_{\lambda_{\rm env}}(\theta_{R})\|_{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>R</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{dist}\bigl(0,\partial F(\hat{\theta}_{R})\bigr)\;\leq\;\|\nabla F_{\lambda_{\rm env}}(\theta_{R})\|_{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p3.4" class="ltx_p">Thus, driving <math id="A4.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\nabla F_{\lambda_{\rm env}}(\theta_{R})\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla F_{\lambda_{\rm env}}(\theta_{R})\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> small (as guaranteed in expectation by Theorem <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 5.2 (Convergence rate for the Moreau envelope). ‣ 5.1 Convergence analysis ‣ 5 Analysis ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.2</span></a>, with sample complexity summarized in Corollary <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem3" title="Corollary 5.3 (Sample complexity for envelope stationarity). ‣ 5.1 Convergence analysis ‣ 5 Analysis ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.3</span></a>) simultaneously guarantees proximity to, and near-stationarity of, a point for the original constrained robust objective.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma D.1</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(What if we do not compute the proximal point?)<span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assume <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="F:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to(-\infty,+\infty]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to(-\infty,+\infty]</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>-weakly convex and bounded below, and fix
<math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}\in(0,1/\kappa)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}\in(0,1/\kappa)</annotation></semantics></math> as in Definition 4.10. For any <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, let</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex120" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex120.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\theta}:=\operatorname{prox}_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}F}(\theta),\qquad\xi:=\nabla F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta)=\frac{1}{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta-\hat{\theta})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>prox</mi><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\theta}:=\operatorname{prox}_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}F}(\theta),\qquad\xi:=\nabla F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta)=\frac{1}{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta-\hat{\theta})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(Definition <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem10" title="Definition 4.10 (Moreau envelope and proximal point). ‣ 4.4 Algorithm development ‣ 4 Proposed Approach ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.10</span></a>and Lemma <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem11" title="Lemma 4.11 (Properties of the Moreau envelope ( , )). ‣ 4.4 Algorithm development ‣ 4 Proposed Approach ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.11</span></a>). Then:</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\theta-\hat{\theta}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\theta-\hat{\theta}\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E46.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}\|\xi\|," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}\|\xi\|,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(46)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E47"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\operatorname{dist}\bigl(0,\partial F(\hat{\theta})\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\operatorname{dist}\bigl(0,\partial F(\hat{\theta})\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E47.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\|\xi\|," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\|\xi\|,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(47)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\operatorname{dist}\bigl(0,\partial F(\theta)\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\operatorname{dist}\bigl(0,\partial F(\theta)\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E48.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq(1-\kappa\lambda_{\mathrm{env}})\|\xi\|." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq(1-\kappa\lambda_{\mathrm{env}})\|\xi\|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(48)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">On the other hand, under <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>-weak convexity alone, there is <em id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">no</em> universal constant <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex121" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex121.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{dist}\bigl(0,\partial F(\theta)\bigr)\;\leq\;C\,\|\nabla F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta)\|\quad\text{for all $\theta$ and all $\kappa$-weakly convex $F$}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">for all </mtext><mi>θ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> and all </mtext><mi>κ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">-weakly convex </mtext><mi>F</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{dist}\bigl(0,\partial F(\theta)\bigr)\;\leq\;C\,\|\nabla F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta)\|\quad\text{for all $\theta$ and all $\kappa$-weakly convex $F$}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(even in the convex case <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa=0</annotation></semantics></math>).</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">We first prove (<a href="#A4.E46" title="Equation 46 ‣ Lemma D.1 (What if we do not compute the proximal point?). ‣ Appendix D On the practical role of the proximal point ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">46</span></a>)–(<a href="#A4.E47" title="Equation 47 ‣ Lemma D.1 (What if we do not compute the proximal point?). ‣ Appendix D On the practical role of the proximal point ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">47</span></a>). By Lemma 4.11 (see also the
first-order optimality condition for the proximal subproblem),</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex122" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex122.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\in\partial F(\hat{\theta})+\frac{1}{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\hat{\theta}-\theta),\qquad\text{equivalently}\qquad\frac{1}{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta-\hat{\theta})\in\partial F(\hat{\theta})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.111em">∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mtext>equivalently</mtext><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">∈</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\in\partial F(\hat{\theta})+\frac{1}{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\hat{\theta}-\theta),\qquad\text{equivalently}\qquad\frac{1}{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta-\hat{\theta})\in\partial F(\hat{\theta}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">With <math id="A4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi:=\frac{1}{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta-\hat{\theta})=\nabla F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi:=\frac{1}{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta-\hat{\theta})=\nabla F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math>,
taking norms yields <math id="A4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\theta-\hat{\theta}\|=\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}\|\xi\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\theta-\hat{\theta}\|=\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}\|\xi\|</annotation></semantics></math>, which is (<a href="#A4.E46" title="Equation 46 ‣ Lemma D.1 (What if we do not compute the proximal point?). ‣ Appendix D On the practical role of the proximal point ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">46</span></a>).
Moreover, since <math id="A4.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi\in\partial F(\hat{\theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">∈</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi\in\partial F(\hat{\theta})</annotation></semantics></math>, we have
<math id="A4.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{dist}\bigl(0,\partial F(\hat{\theta})\bigr)\leq\|\xi\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{dist}\bigl(0,\partial F(\hat{\theta})\bigr)\leq\|\xi\|</annotation></semantics></math>, which is (<a href="#A4.E47" title="Equation 47 ‣ Lemma D.1 (What if we do not compute the proximal point?). ‣ Appendix D On the practical role of the proximal point ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">47</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Next we prove (<a href="#A4.E48" title="Equation 48 ‣ Lemma D.1 (What if we do not compute the proximal point?). ‣ Appendix D On the practical role of the proximal point ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">48</span></a>). By Lemma C.1 (Monotonicity inequality), for every
<math id="A4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in\partial F(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">∈</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in\partial F(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex123" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex123.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle\xi,v\rangle\geq(1-\kappa\lambda_{\mathrm{env}})\|\xi\|^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\xi,v\rangle\geq(1-\kappa\lambda_{\mathrm{env}})\|\xi\|^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">By Cauchy–Schwarz, <math id="A4.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle\xi,v\rangle\leq\|\xi\|\,\|v\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\xi,v\rangle\leq\|\xi\|\,\|v\|</annotation></semantics></math>, hence for every <math id="A4.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in\partial F(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">∈</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in\partial F(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex124" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex124.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|v\|\geq(1-\kappa\lambda_{\mathrm{env}})\|\xi\|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|v\|\geq(1-\kappa\lambda_{\mathrm{env}})\|\xi\|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">Taking the infimum over <math id="A4.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in\partial F(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">∈</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in\partial F(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> gives (<a href="#A4.E48" title="Equation 48 ‣ Lemma D.1 (What if we do not compute the proximal point?). ‣ Appendix D On the practical role of the proximal point ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">48</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">For the stated consequences with the algorithmic output, apply (<a href="#A4.E46" title="Equation 46 ‣ Lemma D.1 (What if we do not compute the proximal point?). ‣ Appendix D On the practical role of the proximal point ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">46</span></a>)–(<a href="#A4.E47" title="Equation 47 ‣ Lemma D.1 (What if we do not compute the proximal point?). ‣ Appendix D On the practical role of the proximal point ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">47</span></a>)
with <math id="A4.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta=\theta_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta=\theta_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\theta}=\hat{\theta}_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\theta}=\hat{\theta}_{R}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex125" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex125.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\theta_{R}-\hat{\theta}_{R}\|^{2}=\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}^{2}\|\nabla F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta_{R})\|^{2},\qquad\operatorname{dist}^{2}\bigl(0,\partial F(\hat{\theta}_{R})\bigr)\leq\|\nabla F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta_{R})\|^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>dist</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>R</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\theta_{R}-\hat{\theta}_{R}\|^{2}=\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}^{2}\|\nabla F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta_{R})\|^{2},\qquad\operatorname{dist}^{2}\bigl(0,\partial F(\hat{\theta}_{R})\bigr)\leq\|\nabla F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta_{R})\|^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">Taking expectations, using Jensen’s inequality for <math id="A4.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\|\theta_{R}-\hat{\theta}_{R}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\|\theta_{R}-\hat{\theta}_{R}\|</annotation></semantics></math>, and
plugging <math id="A4.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\|\nabla F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta_{R})\|^{2}\leq\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\|\nabla F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta_{R})\|^{2}\leq\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> yields the two bounds.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, we show that no universal constant <math id="A4.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> can upper bound
<math id="A4.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{dist}(0,\partial F(\theta))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{dist}(0,\partial F(\theta))</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="A4.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\nabla F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta)\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta)\|</annotation></semantics></math> under weak convexity alone.
Consider <math id="A4.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta=\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta=\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, and define <math id="A4.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(\theta)=|\theta|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(\theta)=|\theta|</annotation></semantics></math>, which is convex (thus <math id="A4.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa=0</annotation></semantics></math>).
Fix <math id="A4.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}=1</annotation></semantics></math> and any <math id="A4.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>. The proximal point is</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex126" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex126.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\theta}=\arg\min_{u\in\mathbb{R}}\Big\{|u|+\tfrac{1}{2}(u-\theta)^{2}\Big\}=0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></munder></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\theta}=\arg\min_{u\in\mathbb{R}}\Big\{|u|+\tfrac{1}{2}(u-\theta)^{2}\Big\}=0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">so <math id="A4.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta)=\theta-\hat{\theta}=\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta)=\theta-\hat{\theta}=\theta</annotation></semantics></math>. However, for <math id="A4.p7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="A4.p7.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial F(\theta)=\{1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial F(\theta)=\{1\}</annotation></semantics></math> and therefore <math id="A4.p7.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{dist}(0,\partial F(\theta))=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{dist}(0,\partial F(\theta))=1</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex127" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex127.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\operatorname{dist}(0,\partial F(\theta))}{\|\nabla F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta)\|}=\frac{1}{\theta}\to\infty\quad\text{as }\theta\downarrow 0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>θ</mi></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext>as </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\operatorname{dist}(0,\partial F(\theta))}{\|\nabla F_{\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}}(\theta)\|}=\frac{1}{\theta}\to\infty\quad\text{as }\theta\downarrow 0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p7.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p7.3.1" class="ltx_text">which rules out any finite universal <math id="A4.p7.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Remark D.2</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> </span>(Interpretation for practice)<span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Even if Algorithm 1 outputs only
<math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> (without solving the proximal subproblem), Theorem 5.2 still certifies that <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> lies within
<math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}\sqrt{\varepsilon})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>ε</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\lambda_{\mathrm{env}}\sqrt{\varepsilon})</annotation></semantics></math> of a point <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\theta}_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\theta}_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> that is <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\sqrt{\varepsilon})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msqrt><mi>ε</mi></msqrt><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\sqrt{\varepsilon})</annotation></semantics></math>-stationary
for the original constrained objective <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math>. In contrast, without additional regularity beyond <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>-weak convexity,
one cannot generally convert envelope stationarity into a bound on <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{dist}(0,\partial F(\theta_{R}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{dist}(0,\partial F(\theta_{R}))</annotation></semantics></math> itself; this is why
the analysis (and the stationarity notion) is phrased in terms of the proximal point.</p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1 </span>Practical computation of the proximal point</h3>

<div id="A4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the analysis we introduce the proximal point</p>
<table id="A4.E49" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\theta}_{R}\;:=\;\operatorname{prox}_{\lambda_{\rm env}}F(\theta_{R})\;=\;\arg\min_{\theta\in\Theta}\Big\{L_{\rho}^{W}(\theta)+\frac{1}{2\lambda_{\rm env}}\|\theta-\theta_{R}\|_{2}^{2}\Big\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>prox</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow></munder></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>ρ</mi><mi>W</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\theta}_{R}\;:=\;\operatorname{prox}_{\lambda_{\rm env}}F(\theta_{R})\;=\;\arg\min_{\theta\in\Theta}\Big\{L_{\rho}^{W}(\theta)+\frac{1}{2\lambda_{\rm env}}\|\theta-\theta_{R}\|_{2}^{2}\Big\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(49)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(\theta):=L_{\rho}^{W}(\theta)+I_{\Theta}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>ρ</mi><mi>W</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(\theta):=L_{\rho}^{W}(\theta)+I_{\Theta}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\rm env}\in(0,1/\kappa)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\rm env}\in(0,1/\kappa)</annotation></semantics></math>.
By weak convexity of <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\rm env}&lt;1/\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\rm env}&lt;1/\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>, the objective in (<a href="#A4.E49" title="Equation 49 ‣ D.1 Practical computation of the proximal point ‣ Appendix D On the practical role of the proximal point ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">49</span></a>)
is strongly convex and hence admits a unique minimizer <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\theta}_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\theta}_{R}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Although Algorithm 1 outputs <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, one can compute an approximation
<math id="A4.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\theta}_{R}\approx\hat{\theta}_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>≈</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\theta}_{R}\approx\hat{\theta}_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> as an optional post-processing step, warm-started at <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{R}</annotation></semantics></math>. A simple inner-loop solver is provided below.</p>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">A simple inner-loop solver.</h4>

<div id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{(0)}:=\theta_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>:=</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{(0)}:=\theta_{R}</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=0,1,\ldots,K-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=0,1,\ldots,K-1</annotation></semantics></math>, sample <math id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z^{(k)}\sim d_{\theta^{(k)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z^{(k)}\sim d_{\theta^{(k)}}</annotation></semantics></math> and compute
the stochastic direction</p>
<table id="A4.Ex128" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex128.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G^{\rm prox}\big(\theta^{(k)};Z^{(k)}\big)\;:=\;G_{\rm SAIL}\big(\theta^{(k)};Z^{(k)}\big)\;+\;\lambda\,G_{R}\big(\theta^{(k)};Z^{(k)}\big)\;+\;\frac{1}{\lambda_{\rm env}}\big(\theta^{(k)}-\theta_{R}\big)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mi>prox</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>SAIL</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G^{\rm prox}\big(\theta^{(k)};Z^{(k)}\big)\;:=\;G_{\rm SAIL}\big(\theta^{(k)};Z^{(k)}\big)\;+\;\lambda\,G_{R}\big(\theta^{(k)};Z^{(k)}\big)\;+\;\frac{1}{\lambda_{\rm env}}\big(\theta^{(k)}-\theta_{R}\big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">which is the usual oracle from Assumption 6 plus the deterministic gradient of the proximal quadratic.
Then take a projected step</p>
<table id="A4.E50" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{(k+1)}\;:=\;\Pi_{\Theta}\!\left(\theta^{(k)}-\alpha_{k}\,G^{\rm prox}\big(\theta^{(k)};Z^{(k)}\big)\right),\qquad\bar{\theta}_{R}:=\theta^{(K)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mi>prox</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{(k+1)}\;:=\;\Pi_{\Theta}\!\left(\theta^{(k)}-\alpha_{k}\,G^{\rm prox}\big(\theta^{(k)};Z^{(k)}\big)\right),\qquad\bar{\theta}_{R}:=\theta^{(K)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(50)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Since the proximal quadratic improves conditioning, this inner loop is typically stable in practice.
Moreover, the theory only requires <math id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\theta}_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\theta}_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> to be a sufficiently accurate approximation;
exact solves of (<a href="#A4.E49" title="Equation 49 ‣ D.1 Practical computation of the proximal point ‣ Appendix D On the practical role of the proximal point ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">49</span></a>) are not necessary. This is consistent with standard practice in inexact proximal methods, where the proximal subproblem is solved
only approximately while maintaining meaningful convergence guarantees (e.g., <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">Schmidt et al. 45</a></cite>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma D.3</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Stationarity of an inexact proximal point)<span id="A4.Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\rm env}\in(0,1/\kappa)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\rm env}\in(0,1/\kappa)</annotation></semantics></math> and an index <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\theta}_{R}=\operatorname{prox}_{\lambda_{\rm env}}F(\theta_{R})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>prox</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\theta}_{R}=\operatorname{prox}_{\lambda_{\rm env}}F(\theta_{R})</annotation></semantics></math> and let <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\theta}_{R}\in\Theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\theta}_{R}\in\Theta</annotation></semantics></math> be any point.
Define the proximal objective</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex129" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex129.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi_{R}(\theta)\;:=\;F(\theta)+\frac{1}{2\lambda_{\rm env}}\|\theta-\theta_{R}\|_{2}^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi_{R}(\theta)\;:=\;F(\theta)+\frac{1}{2\lambda_{\rm env}}\|\theta-\theta_{R}\|_{2}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\theta}_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\theta}_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies the (first-order) proximal residual bound</span></p>
<table id="A4.E51" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{dist}\!\left(0,\partial\Psi_{R}(\bar{\theta}_{R})\right)\;\leq\;\varepsilon_{\rm prox}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.525em;" width="1.525em"><mi>dist</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>R</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>prox</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{dist}\!\left(0,\partial\Psi_{R}(\bar{\theta}_{R})\right)\;\leq\;\varepsilon_{\rm prox},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(51)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">then</span></p>
<table id="A4.E52" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{dist}\!\left(0,\partial F(\bar{\theta}_{R})\right)\;\leq\;\|\nabla F_{\lambda_{\rm env}}(\theta_{R})\|_{2}\;+\;\varepsilon_{\rm prox}\;+\;\frac{1}{\lambda_{\rm env}}\|\bar{\theta}_{R}-\hat{\theta}_{R}\|_{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.525em;" width="1.525em"><mi>dist</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>R</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>prox</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{dist}\!\left(0,\partial F(\bar{\theta}_{R})\right)\;\leq\;\|\nabla F_{\lambda_{\rm env}}(\theta_{R})\|_{2}\;+\;\varepsilon_{\rm prox}\;+\;\frac{1}{\lambda_{\rm env}}\|\bar{\theta}_{R}-\hat{\theta}_{R}\|_{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(52)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In particular, if one ensures <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\bar{\theta}_{R}-\hat{\theta}_{R}\|_{2}\leq\lambda_{\rm env}\varepsilon_{\rm geom}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>geom</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\bar{\theta}_{R}-\hat{\theta}_{R}\|_{2}\leq\lambda_{\rm env}\varepsilon_{\rm geom}</annotation></semantics></math>,
then
<math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{dist}\!\left(0,\partial F(\bar{\theta}_{R})\right)\leq\|\nabla F_{\lambda_{\rm env}}(\theta_{R})\|_{2}+\varepsilon_{\rm prox}+\varepsilon_{\rm geom}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.525em;" width="1.525em"><mi>dist</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>R</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>prox</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>geom</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{dist}\!\left(0,\partial F(\bar{\theta}_{R})\right)\leq\|\nabla F_{\lambda_{\rm env}}(\theta_{R})\|_{2}+\varepsilon_{\rm prox}+\varepsilon_{\rm geom}.</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">By subdifferential calculus,
<math id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial\Psi_{R}(\theta)=\partial F(\theta)+\frac{1}{\lambda_{\rm env}}(\theta-\theta_{R})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial\Psi_{R}(\theta)=\partial F(\theta)+\frac{1}{\lambda_{\rm env}}(\theta-\theta_{R}).</annotation></semantics></math>
The residual condition (<a href="#A4.E51" title="Equation 51 ‣ Lemma D.3 (Stationarity of an inexact proximal point). ‣ A simple inner-loop solver. ‣ D.1 Practical computation of the proximal point ‣ Appendix D On the practical role of the proximal point ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">51</span></a>) implies there exists
<math id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\in\partial F(\bar{\theta}_{R})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">∈</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>R</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\in\partial F(\bar{\theta}_{R})</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex130" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex130.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|g+\frac{1}{\lambda_{\rm env}}(\bar{\theta}_{R}-\theta_{R})\right\|_{2}\;\leq\;\varepsilon_{\rm prox}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>prox</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|g+\frac{1}{\lambda_{\rm env}}(\bar{\theta}_{R}-\theta_{R})\right\|_{2}\;\leq\;\varepsilon_{\rm prox}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex131" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex131.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{dist}\!\left(0,\partial F(\bar{\theta}_{R})\right)\;\leq\;\|g\|_{2}\;\leq\;\varepsilon_{\rm prox}+\frac{1}{\lambda_{\rm env}}\|\bar{\theta}_{R}-\theta_{R}\|_{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.525em;" width="1.525em"><mi>dist</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>R</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>prox</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{dist}\!\left(0,\partial F(\bar{\theta}_{R})\right)\;\leq\;\|g\|_{2}\;\leq\;\varepsilon_{\rm prox}+\frac{1}{\lambda_{\rm env}}\|\bar{\theta}_{R}-\theta_{R}\|_{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">Next, by the triangle inequality,
<math id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\bar{\theta}_{R}-\theta_{R}\|_{2}\leq\|\bar{\theta}_{R}-\hat{\theta}_{R}\|_{2}+\|\hat{\theta}_{R}-\theta_{R}\|_{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\bar{\theta}_{R}-\theta_{R}\|_{2}\leq\|\bar{\theta}_{R}-\hat{\theta}_{R}\|_{2}+\|\hat{\theta}_{R}-\theta_{R}\|_{2}.</annotation></semantics></math>
By Lemma 4.11 (property <math id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla F_{\lambda_{\rm env}}(\theta)=\frac{1}{\lambda_{\rm env}}(\theta-\operatorname{prox}_{\lambda_{\rm env}}F(\theta))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>prox</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla F_{\lambda_{\rm env}}(\theta)=\frac{1}{\lambda_{\rm env}}(\theta-\operatorname{prox}_{\lambda_{\rm env}}F(\theta))</annotation></semantics></math>),
we have <math id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\hat{\theta}_{R}-\theta_{R}\|_{2}=\lambda_{\rm env}\|\nabla F_{\lambda_{\rm env}}(\theta_{R})\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>env</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\hat{\theta}_{R}-\theta_{R}\|_{2}=\lambda_{\rm env}\|\nabla F_{\lambda_{\rm env}}(\theta_{R})\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Substituting yields (<a href="#A4.E52" title="Equation 52 ‣ Lemma D.3 (Stationarity of an inexact proximal point). ‣ A simple inner-loop solver. ‣ D.1 Practical computation of the proximal point ‣ Appendix D On the practical role of the proximal point ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">52</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Remark D.4</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> </span>(Practical stopping criteria.)<span id="A4.Thmtheorem4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Lemma <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma D.3 (Stationarity of an inexact proximal point). ‣ A simple inner-loop solver. ‣ D.1 Practical computation of the proximal point ‣ Appendix D On the practical role of the proximal point ‣ Oracle-Robust Online Alignment for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.3</span></a> suggests two inexpensive targets for the inner loop:
(i) keep the proximal residual <math id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{dist}(0,\partial\Psi_{R}(\theta^{(k)}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{dist}(0,\partial\Psi_{R}(\theta^{(k)}))</annotation></semantics></math> small (as estimated by a minibatch),
and (ii) exploit warm-starting so that <math id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\bar{\theta}_{R}-\hat{\theta}_{R}\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\bar{\theta}_{R}-\hat{\theta}_{R}\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> remains modest.</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
